stateDiagram-v2
%% Coda physician web app: the one unified behavior graph (rewrite, 2026-10-23).
%% The graph is the spec; Verus derives from it. It states ideal product behavior from Dev's
%% intent and the settled sources, never from existing code.
%% Its limits follow the Charter and the communication standard in decisions.md: every limit
%% says what it protects, and everything Coda judges is a "may".
%%
%% Events. Every labeled step carries a declared event: who causes it, what it needs, and
%% what it is for. Physician commands need an active session (bug 15 becomes structural).
%% events declared
%% event sign in to the practice | by you | You open your emailed sign-in link: a member lands on Today, and a link that no longer grants access to this practice says so. Asking for a link never reveals whether an account exists; an address without one is sent nothing (Dev 2026-10-24).
%% event sign in through a link | by you | You sign in from a Coda link to a patient or an item: a member lands on that patient with exactly the access they have, and the link then opens its item; anyone else is refused. The sign-in email carries no patient; the place stays with the Coda link (Dev 2026-10-24; sign-in.mmd, Patient link).
%% event open the patient | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | You open the patient: their page, identity only, or a not-available notice, by your access.
%% event follow a link | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | A Coda link opened while signed in lands on its patient by your access, then opens its item.
%% event try another account | by you | You leave the refusal and return to the sign-in page.
%% event sign out | by you | You end your session; nothing about patient work changes.
%% event practice access removed | by the practice | The practice removes this physician; any open session ends and later sign-ins are refused.
%% event practice access granted | by the practice | The practice makes this account a member.
%% event the session expires | by the session | A sign-in prompt covers the screen and hides patient content; nothing underneath changes.
%% event sign in again | by you | You open the sign-in link the prompt emailed you: the covered page and the link's own page are both back exactly where you were (Dev 2026-10-24).
%% event a different physician signs in | by you | Another physician's sign-in link opens here: your session ends and theirs starts at Today; drafts and seen state stay with each physician (N7, Dev 2026-10-24). Your own link changes nothing.
%% event reopen Coda after the session ended | by you | You come back after the session ended while Coda was closed: the sign-in page shows, and signing in opens Today (Dev 2026-10-24).
%% event identity access granted | by the practice | The physician may now see who the patient is, nothing clinical.
%% event clinical access granted | by the practice | The physician may now see the patient's clinical content.
%% event clinical access reduced | by the practice | The physician keeps identity access only; clinical content closes.
%% event patient access removed | by the practice | The physician can no longer see the patient; everything showing the patient closes.
%% event go to Today | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | You return to Today, the list of what needs you.
%% event open all updates | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | Coda opens on Updates, the record of everything Coda did.
%% event open find patient | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | You open the roster search.
%% event close find patient | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | You close the search.
%% event type in find patient | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | Each change searches the whole roster on the server.
%%
%% Coda's work: one lifecycle for every kind (rewrite-worklist "Ideal behavior: Coda's work").
%% Causes are other owners' events; they make work owed. Starting waits for what the work needs.
%% events news for the patient = new records arrive | a shared Duet record arrives | the patient sends For my doctor | the patient joins and consents | a message arrives from a known sender | the patient writes again | confirm the match | link the message to the patient | the practice replies in the channel
%% events the concern is shown = open the concern | the link opens the concern
%% events message news = a message arrives from a known sender | the patient sends For my doctor | the patient writes again | confirm the match | link the message to the patient | the practice replies in the channel | the correction's Undo ends
%% event new records arrive | by the records source | needs SrcConnecting, SrcCurrent, SrcFailed, SrcBack | reason: records arrive only from a connected source | New records for the patient are available to read; a source that couldn't update, or is back but not yet updated, is current again.
%% event a shared Duet record arrives | by the patient through Duet | needs PcConnected | reason: connected means sharing; nothing arrives otherwise | The patient shares something new through Duet.
%% event the patient sends For my doctor | by the patient through Duet | needs PcConnected | reason: a patient sends only to the practice they're connected to | The patient's own For my doctor arrives, linked to them like a message from a known sender; Coda's agents read it and judge whether a physician needs to see it (Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event a patient message arrives | by the messaging channel | needs ChLive | reason: only a live channel delivers messages | A message from an unknown sender reaches the practice; Coda suggests a patient, and a person confirms before it becomes evidence (PM-500).
%% event the follow-up comes due | by the follow-up's date | needs FWaiting | reason: only an active follow-up comes due | A follow-up's date arrives, so Coda reviews what it was for.
%% event the weekly cycle comes round | by the practice calendar | The weekly look across the patient comes due.
%% event the visit comes into preparation range | by the practice schedule | needs VLater, VmMapped | reason: only a scheduled visit linked to the patient is prepared | An upcoming visit is close enough to prepare for (how far ahead is practice policy).
%% event ask Coda to reply | by you | command on the reply: Ask Coda to reply, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, MLLinked, ChAccount, MRRest | reason: only a linked conversation on a connected channel with no reply open can ask for one (X4, px.md:167) | You ask Coda to draft a reply; it waits behind a patient review already running, and a reply that review proposes first answers the ask (px.md:167; Dev 2026-10-24).
%% event Coda decides to take something on | by Coda | Coda judges something worth doing for the patient and takes it on (charter: Coda may).
%% event Coda starts the {work} | by Coda | needs WOwed@{key} | reason: only the work's own state makes its events possible | Coda begins the {work} from the latest evidence it may read.
%% event the {work} fails | by Coda's runtime | needs WRun@{key} | reason: only the work's own state makes its events possible | The {work} couldn't finish after whatever recovery the runtime does on its own; it shows Couldn't finish with Try again, and machinery never alerts you (CT:95).
%% event Coda finishes the {work} with an update for you | by Coda | needs WRun@{key}, NwNone@{key}, MLFree | reason: only the work's own state makes its events possible, work takes in what arrived while it ran before it finishes (Dev 2026-10-26), and work waits out a correction's Undo (PM:552-559) | The {work} ends from current records and writes you an update in Updates. Only such a finish raises or revises a concern, which it explains (care-team contract, visibility table; Dev 2026-10-26); every other effect is a may: a concern raised, revised or closed, a question for you kept with one active follow-up (CT:104), a reply draft, a follow-up change, or change notices.
%% event Coda finishes the {work} quietly | by Coda | needs WRun@{key}, NwNone@{key}, MLFree | reason: only the work's own state makes its events possible, work takes in what arrived while it ran before it finishes (Dev 2026-10-26), and work waits out a correction's Undo (PM:552-559) | The {work} ends from current records and writes you nothing; quiet in Updates. It may close concerns but never raises or revises one; every other effect is a may: a question for you kept with one active follow-up (CT:104), a reply draft, a follow-up change, or change notices.
%% events Coda finishes the {work} = Coda finishes the {work} with an update for you | Coda finishes the {work} quietly
%% event Coda waits on the {work} for missing information | by Coda | needs WRun@{key} | reason: only the work's own state makes its events possible | Coda keeps the {work} for information that will arrive anyway; the patient page shows Waiting with the reason and Try again, never Today.
%% event Coda can't restart the {work} | by Coda's runtime | needs WOwed@{key}, WFail@{key} | reason: only the work's own state makes its events possible | The {work} can't run again; anything left goes to Today with Done, otherwise Updates logs it. It never blocks later work.
%% event try the {work} again | by you | command on the {work}: Try again, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, WFail@{key}, WWait@{key} | reason: only stalled work offers Try again | You retry the {work}; it reads the latest records and stays in its episode.
%% event stop the {held} | by you | command on the {held}: Stop, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, WHand@{key} | reason: only work in hand can be stopped | You stop the {held}; it is held with Resume where you stopped it.
%% event stop and discuss the {held} | by you | command on the {held}: Stop and discuss, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, WHand@{key} | reason: only work in hand can be stopped | You stop the {held} and open a conversation that can change what it carried.
%% event resume the {held} | by you | command on the {held}: Resume, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, HYes@{key} | reason: only held work resumes | The held {held} runs again from a fresh read (N8).
%% event mark the {left} done | by you | command on the {left}: Done on what's left, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, LShown@{key} | reason: only a row on Today can be marked done | You clear what the {left} left for you.
%% event Coda takes in what arrived in the {work} | by Coda | needs WRun@{key}, NwSeen@{key} | reason: only running work takes in what arrived while it ran | Coda notices what arrived while it worked and takes it in before it finishes, so nothing it publishes rests on an older reading; the patient review still owns responding to news (Dev 2026-10-26).
%% event update the {fresh} with the newer records | by you | command on the {fresh}: Update, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, WDoneStale@{key} | reason: only an answer with newer records since offers Update | One tap answers again on the newer records (Dev 2026-10-26).
%%
%% Outcomes. Every kind of work ends with one event; what it produces is each owner's "may".
%% events Coda finishes any work = Coda finishes the {work} with an update for you | Coda finishes the {work} quietly
%% events Coda finishes any work with an update for you = Coda finishes the {work} with an update for you
%% event open the concern | by you | needs SIn, AClin | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access | You read the concern; opening is yours alone and never clears it.
%% event another physician opens the concern | by another physician | Someone else read it; it stays new to you.
%% event mark the concern done | by you | command on the concern: Done, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, CNeeds | reason: Done needs clinical access and a concern that needs attention | Done clears this exact concern for every physician (Dev 2026-10-22).
%% event another physician marks the concern done | by another physician | Done by anyone clears it for everyone.
%% event create a follow-up | by you | command on the follow-up: Create, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, FNone, FCompleted, FCancelled | reason: a new follow-up needs none active or held | You set up a follow-up: what to check and when.
%% event change the follow-up | by you | command on the follow-up: Change, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, FActive, FHeld | reason: only an active or held follow-up changes | You change it, even while stopped; a due occurrence's owed review ends, and it comes due again on its own if still due.
%% event review the follow-up now | by you | command on the follow-up: Review now, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, FActive | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access; held work uses Resume (CT:612) | One review of the current follow-up; work already in hand is reused.
%% event stop the follow-up | by you | command on the follow-up: Stop, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, FActive | reason: only an active follow-up stops | You stop the follow-up; it and its review hold until Resume (M1).
%% event stop and discuss the follow-up | by you | command on the follow-up: Stop and discuss, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, FActive | reason: only an active follow-up stops | You stop the follow-up and open a conversation about it; it holds until Resume.
%% event resume the follow-up | by you | command on the follow-up: Resume, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, FHeld | reason: only a held follow-up resumes | Resume reviews the current version of the follow-up (M1).
%% event cancel the follow-up | by you | command on the follow-up: Cancel, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, FActive, FHeld | reason: only an active or held follow-up is cancelled | You end the follow-up; Coda respects the cancel unless new information arrives (A5).
%% event complete the follow-up | by you | command on the follow-up: Complete, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, FActive, FHeld | reason: only an active or held follow-up is completed | You mark it complete, offered with new date or cancel when Coda can't restart its review (A4).
%% events Coda finishes other work = Coda finishes the initial understanding with an update for you | Coda finishes the initial understanding quietly | Coda finishes the patient review with an update for you | Coda finishes the patient review quietly | Coda finishes the weekly review with an update for you | Coda finishes the weekly review quietly | Coda finishes the visit preparation with an update for you | Coda finishes the visit preparation quietly | Coda finishes the asked reply with an update for you | Coda finishes the asked reply quietly | Coda finishes the proactive work with an update for you | Coda finishes the proactive work quietly | Coda finishes the answer with an update for you | Coda finishes the answer quietly | Coda finishes the reply revision with an update for you | Coda finishes the reply revision quietly
%% event a visit is scheduled | by the practice schedule | needs VNone, VOver, VCancel | reason: one visit is modeled at a time | A new visit for the patient is on the schedule.
%% event the visit ends | by the clock | needs VAhead, VCancelled | reason: only a visit still ahead can pass | The visit's recorded time passes; a running preparation finishes, anything owed or failed ends.
%% event the visit is cancelled | by the practice schedule | needs VAhead | reason: only a visit still ahead can be cancelled | Everything unfinished for that visit ends at once; a finished briefing stays as history.
%% event the visit is moved | by the practice schedule | needs VAhead | reason: only a visit still ahead can move | Everything unfinished for the old time ends; the new time is prepared fresh.
%% event the practice's visit reaches the patient's Duet | by the practice schedule | needs PcConnected, VAhead | reason: the schedule reaches only a connected patient's Duet, and only for a visit still ahead | A visit already on the schedule when the patient joins shows in their Duet; nothing changes here.
%% event the link opens the concern | by the app | needs AClin | reason: clinical content needs clinical access | The link lands on the concern, read in the reader over the patient page.
%% event the link opens the briefing | by the app | needs AClin | reason: clinical content needs clinical access | The link lands on the briefing.
%% event the link opens the follow-up | by the app | needs AClin | reason: clinical content needs clinical access | The link lands on the follow-up.
%% event the link opens past work | by the app | needs AClin | reason: clinical content needs clinical access | The link lands on the piece of Coda's past work.
%% event the link shows the patient page | by the app | The link was to the patient, or its item can't be shown with your access; you stay on the page access allows.
%% event open the briefing | by you | needs SIn, AClin, BReady, BOld | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access; only an existing briefing opens | You read the briefing in the reader.
%% event open the follow-up | by you | needs SIn, AClin, FActive, FHeld, FCompleted, FCancelled | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access; only an existing follow-up opens | You read the follow-up in the reader.
%% event open past work | by you | needs SIn, AClin | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access | You read a piece of Coda's past work.
%% event open past work from the follow-up | by you | needs SIn, AClin, RFollow | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access | From a follow-up you open the work that set or changed it.
%% event open the work that raised the concern | by you | needs SIn, AClin, RConcern | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access | From a concern you open the work that raised or last revised it; that work always has the written communication explaining the concern (CT visibility: a new or revised concern never comes without one). The link is a data promise for a linked proof.
%% event close the reader | by you | You close the reader and are exactly where you were.
%% event open Updates | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | You open the day's log of everything Coda did.
%% event open the reply | by you | needs SIn, AClin, MROpen | reason: replies are clinical content; only open reply work has a card | You open the reply card from Today, Updates or Past work (Review reply, patient-messaging.md:1128); opening is yours alone, per exact version, and asserts no clinical review (px.md:140, 317).
%% event open the {row} that couldn't restart | by you | needs SIn, AClin, LShown@{key} | reason: clinical content; only a row on Today opens | You open the row; it stays on Today with Done; opening is yours alone, per exact version, and asserts no clinical review (px.md:140, 317).
%% event discuss what you're reading | by you | needs SIn, AClin, ROpen | reason: Discuss belongs to the item open in the reader, which is clinical content | The reader's one primary action opens or returns to that item's exact anchored conversation in this patient, keeping other drafts (px.md:514, 695).
%% event open an update | by you | needs SIn, AClin | reason: commands need an active session; an update about a patient is clinical content | You read one update, from the Updates list or wherever the app offers it; opening records it seen and never removes it. Previewing one never navigates or clears attention; only opening it does (PX).
%% event back to Updates | by you | You return to the list where you were.
%% event close Updates | by you | You close the panel.
%% event {read} shows a saved copy | by the app | needs RdLoading@{key} | reason: only a read in progress shows a saved copy | What you saw last appears at once and refreshes quietly; loading shows only when nothing can.
%% event {read} loads | by the practice system | A first read shows; a refresh updates what is shown in place, and an empty answer never replaces it (px.md:990).
%% event {read} loads in part | by the practice system | What loaded shows with one quiet line and Retry; never read as empty (RP-217).
%% event {read} fails to load | by the practice system | What was shown stays with one quiet line and Retry; with nothing shown, it says it couldn't load, with Retry (px.md:440).
%% event retry {read} | by you | needs SIn, RdKept@{key}, RdFailed@{key} | reason: only a read that shows a problem offers Retry | You read it again; what is shown stays.
%% event go to an earlier day | by you | needs SIn, RdShown@day, RdKept@day | reason: Earlier comes from a read that named an earlier day (runtime-protocol.md:418) | You step back to the latest earlier day with rows you may see (PX-437).
%% event return to today's updates | by you | needs SIn, UwEarlier | reason: Today shows only on an earlier day | You come back to today.
%% event go to the next update | by you | needs SIn, AClin, UReading | reason: an update about a patient is clinical content | The reader steps to the next update, passing over conversation rows (px.md:432).
%% event go to the previous update | by you | needs SIn, AClin, UReading | reason: an update about a patient is clinical content | The reader steps to the previous update, passing over conversation rows (px.md:432).
%% event the practice connects a calendar | by the practice | needs ScOff@schedule | reason: only a practice without a calendar connects one | The schedule rail appears beside the list.
%% event the schedule finds no calendar | by the practice system | There is no schedule to show (px.md:613).
%% event midnight passes | by the practice clock | The practice day turns over: Today, Updates on today and the schedule refresh in place, a read that failed tries again, and each patient's update for today starts over (runtime-protocol.md:174-182).
%%
%% The conversation. Coda's answer is one more kind of work above. Send while Coda answers steers
%% it; Send next queues (Dev 2026-10-23). Stop pauses the queue: a queued message starts only once the
%% answer is no longer in progress and not held, so Resume continues the answer and then the queue
%% (A1, Codex desktop). A failed answer releases the queue (BUG 12). Typed text is never lost (N3).
%% event open a conversation | by you | needs SIn, AClin | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access | You open one of the patient's conversations.
%% event start a new conversation | by you | needs SIn, AClin | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access | You start a fresh conversation about the patient.
%% event start dictation | by you | needs SIn | reason: dictation is the composer's own, local until it stops | Hold the shortcut or click the microphone beside Send; existing text stays visible.
%% event the microphone is allowed | by the browser | Recording starts, with live input levels and a stop control.
%% event the microphone is refused | by the browser | Nothing is recorded; your text is kept.
%% event release before permission | by you | Letting go before the browser answers cancels that attempt instead of recording later.
%% event stop recording | by you | The completed recording goes for transcription; nothing is sent before stop.
%% event cancel dictation | by you | Escape or stop cancels capture or processing and fences late results; your text is kept.
%% event the transcript is inserted | by the transcription service | The literal transcript lands at your original selection, the target unchanged; it saves like typing.
%% event the transcript arrives for a changed target | by the transcription service | You moved or edited meanwhile, so it waits as a preview for you to insert at your cursor.
%% event insert the transcript | by you | needs SIn, CrNone@conversation, RdShown@conversation, RdKept@conversation | reason: dictation is the composer's own; a composer opens only once its conversation and saved draft are shown, so nothing typed hides the saved text | You place the preview at your cursor; it saves like typing.
%% event transcription fails | by the transcription service | Your text is kept; no audio is stored or retried (px.md:349-350).
%% events you lose clinical access = clinical access reduced | patient access removed | practice access removed
%% events you stop the follow-up = stop the follow-up | stop and discuss the follow-up
%% events you stop the {held} = stop the {held} | stop and discuss the {held}
%% events you change the Updates day = go to an earlier day | return to today's updates
%% events another update opens = go to the next update | go to the previous update | open an update
%% events you write to Coda = send | send to steer the answer | send next | send a queued message now
%% events access to the patient narrows = clinical access reduced | patient access removed
%% events you open a conversation = open a conversation | discuss what you're reading | stop and discuss the {held} | stop and discuss the follow-up
%% events you leave the conversation = go to Today | open the patient | start a new conversation | follow a link | clinical access reduced | patient access removed
%% events you leave the composer = go to Today | open the patient | open a conversation | start a new conversation | follow a link | discuss what you're reading | clinical access reduced | patient access removed | the session expires
%% event type in the composer | by you | needs SIn, CrNone@conversation, RdShown@conversation, RdKept@conversation | reason: a composer opens only once its conversation and saved draft are shown, so nothing typed hides the saved text | Your draft saves quietly as you write.
%% event the draft saves | by the practice system | A draft that showed Not saved is kept again, for you alone; quiet saving shows nothing.
%% event the draft fails to save | by the practice system | The draft shows Not saved with Retry; nothing else stops.
%% event retry saving the draft | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | You retry the save.
%% event discard the draft | by you | needs SIn, CrNone@conversation, RdShown@conversation, RdKept@conversation | reason: a composer opens only once its conversation and saved draft are shown, so nothing typed hides the saved text | You clear the draft on purpose.
%% event send | by you | command on the conversation: Send, clicked while SIn, DText, CrNone@conversation, RdShown@conversation, RdKept@conversation | needs AClin, WIdle@answer, WStalled@answer | reason: a message needs clinical access, and while Coda answers it steers or waits as Send next instead; only written text sends | Your message starts Coda's answer; it supersedes a stopped answer's Resume. It sends even when autosave failed (A2). Writing on the patient page opens a new conversation (PX-897).
%% event send to steer the answer | by you | command on the conversation: Steer, clicked while SIn, DText, CrNone@conversation, RdShown@conversation, RdKept@conversation, WRun@answer | needs AClin | reason: Steer shows only while an answer runs, and one that arrives after the answer finished starts a new answer (runtime-protocol.md:1519) | Your message joins the answer in progress at once (Dev 2026-10-24).
%% event send next | by you | command on the conversation: Send next, clicked while SIn, DText, CrNone@conversation, RdShown@conversation, RdKept@conversation, WActive@answer | needs AClin | reason: Send next shows only while an answer is in progress, and one that arrives after it ended starts a new answer (runtime-protocol.md:1519) | Your message waits, editable, for the next answer.
%% event edit a queued message | by you | command on the queued messages: Edit, clicked while SIn | needs QQueued | reason: only a waiting message can be edited | You change a waiting message.
%% event remove a queued message | by you | command on the queued messages: Remove, clicked while SIn | needs QQueued | reason: only a waiting message can be removed | The message leaves the queue and its text returns to your draft without overwriting newer text.
%% event send a queued message now | by you | command on the queued messages: Send now, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, QQueued, WIdle@answer, WStalled@answer | reason: a queued message is sent at once only while no answer is in progress, as after Stop; during an answer it waits its turn (A1 revised; runtime-protocol.md:1515) | That message starts the next answer now, ahead of Resume; the others stay queued.
%% event the queued message starts | by the app | needs QQueued, WIdle@answer, WStalled@answer, HNo@answer | reason: queued messages wait until the answer is no longer in progress and not held by Stop (A1) | The waiting messages start the next answer.
%% event archive the conversation | by you | command on the conversation: Archive, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, CoActive, WIdle@answer, WFail@answer, QNone | reason: one eligibility rule for the button and the command: no active answer, queued message, or pending continuation (runtime-protocol.md:499) | The conversation leaves the active list; its history, work and attention are unchanged.
%% event restore the conversation | by you | command on the conversation: Restore, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, CoArchived | reason: only an archived conversation restores | It returns to the active list and starts no work.
%% event undo the archive | by you | command on the conversation: Undo, clicked while SIn, ArShown | needs AClin, CoArchived | reason: Undo is exact Restore of the archive it names, even after navigation (px.md:386) | The conversation returns to the active list.
%% event the archive notice closes | by the app | needs ArShown | reason: only a shown notice closes | Conversation archived · Undo goes away.
%% event rate the message up | by you | command on the feedback: Thumbs up, clicked while SIn | needs AClin | reason: feedback is about clinical communication; repeating the current rating keeps its details (runtime-protocol.md:508) | The rating saves at once and the optional details open.
%% event rate the message down | by you | command on the feedback: Thumbs down, clicked while SIn | needs AClin | reason: feedback is about clinical communication; repeating the current rating keeps its details (runtime-protocol.md:508) | The rating saves at once and the optional details open.
%% event edit the feedback details | by you | needs SIn, FmOpen | reason: only an open form takes reasons and a note | You pick reasons or write a note; nothing saves yet.
%% event save the feedback details | by you | command on the feedback: Save details, clicked while SIn, FmEdited | needs AClin, FbUp, FbDown | reason: details belong to a saved rating | Your reasons and note save as a new revision.
%% event close the feedback form | by you | needs FmOpen | reason: only an open form closes | The rating stays; unsaved edits are discarded.
%% event open a citation in the reader | by you | needs SIn, AClin, ROpen | reason: sources are clinical content | A citation opens its preview in the reader's pane; opening evidence never clears attention.
%% event open a citation in Updates | by you | needs SIn, AClin, UReading | reason: sources are clinical content | A citation in an update opens its preview.
%% event open a citation in the patient summary | by you | needs SIn, AClin, PPatient | reason: sources are clinical content | A citation in the summary opens its preview on the page.
%% event open a citation in the conversation | by you | needs SIn, AClin, PConv | reason: sources are clinical content | A citation in an answer opens its preview.
%% event go to a source from Sources | by you | needs SIn, AClin, PPatient | reason: sources are clinical content | A row in the patient page's Sources opens that source's first citation (PX 2026-09-17).
%% event expand the source | by you | needs SIn, AClin | reason: sources are clinical content | Expand adds the qualified source text.
%% event the source loads | by the practice system | The source text shows.
%% event the source fails to load | by the practice system | The preview stays, with Retry.
%% event the source has no qualified text | by the practice system | Only the preview can be shown.
%% event retry the source | by you | needs SIn | reason: commands need an active session | You retry the source.
%% event close the source | by you | The pane closes; the surface stays.
%% event the records source can't update | by the records source | needs SrcCurrent, SrcBack | reason: only a source with current or reconnected records can fall behind | "Records couldn't be updated"; Coda keeps working from the last good records. How often the runtime checks and retries is not the graph's (Dev 2026-10-24; infrastructure-gaps.md).
%% event the records source updates again | by the records source | needs SrcFailed, SrcBack | reason: only a source that couldn't update, or is back but not yet updated, recovers | Records are current again; with nothing new, no review follows.
%% event the source becomes unavailable | by the records source | The patient's source is down; their page and briefing say "Records as of …, couldn't update", and Today shows no row for it.
%% event the source is reconnected | by the records source | needs SrcGoneKept, SrcGoneEmpty, PsUp | reason: only an unavailable source reconnects, and not while the practice's whole source is down | The source is back; a check runs at once.
%% event the practice's records source goes down | by the records source | The whole source is down for the practice: one line on Today for the practice, never a row per patient; every patient's records read as unavailable and Coda keeps working from the last good records.
%% event the practice's records source comes back | by the records source | The Today line goes away and every patient's records are checked at once.
%% event invite the patient | by you | command on the patient's connection: Invite, clicked while SIn | needs ADemo, AClin, PcNone, PcEnded | reason: only a patient not connected or invited can be invited; acting on a patient needs you to see them, at least who they are | Any practice member invites a roster patient to connect through Duet, by text with email as backup.
%% event the invitation is delivered | by the messaging provider | needs PcSending | reason: only a sending invitation is delivered | The patient has the invitation.
%% event the invitation can't be delivered | by the messaging provider | needs PcSending | reason: only a sending invitation can fail | The roster shows it couldn't be delivered, with Resend.
%% event resend the invitation | by you | command on the patient's connection: Resend, clicked while SIn | needs ADemo, AClin, PcSent, PcUndelivered | reason: only a sent or undelivered invitation is resent; acting on a patient needs you to see them, at least who they are | A resend replaces the earlier invitation.
%% event the invitation reminder goes out | by the practice system | needs PcFresh | reason: one reminder only | One reminder, then expiry.
%% event the invitation expires | by the practice system | needs PcReminded | reason: an invitation expires after its reminder | The invitation lapses; the patient can be invited again.
%% event cancel the invitation | by you | command on the patient's connection: Cancel the invitation, clicked while SIn | needs ADemo, AClin, PcInvited | reason: only an open invitation is withdrawn; acting on a patient needs you to see them, at least who they are | You withdraw the invitation.
%% event the patient joins and consents | by the patient through Duet | needs PcInvited | reason: any invitation the practice still holds open can be accepted, even while it is being resent (Dev 2026-10-25) | Duet owns joining and consent; connected means sharing, so everything the patient already shares arrives with the join, on a first join and on joining again.
%% event the patient leaves the practice | by the patient through Duet | needs PcConnected | reason: only a live connection can end | The connection ends at once; the practice keeps what it already received, dated.
%% event discharge the patient | by you | command on the patient's connection: Discharge, clicked while SIn | needs ADemo, AClin, PcConnected | reason: only a live connection can end; acting on a patient needs you to see them, at least who they are | Any practice member ends the connection; what was received stays, dated.
%% event the patient's account is deleted | by the patient through Duet | The connection or invitation ends at once; the practice keeps what it already received, dated.
%%
%% Patient messaging (PM). Coda never sends on its own: you copy a reply and send it in Gmail or
%% Spruce, or Send has Coda send exactly your approved words for you, shown as sent by Coda for you
%% (Dev 2026-10-24; PM:160). Accepted, sent, delivered and read are distinct (PM:161).
%% event connect the channel | by you | needs SIn, ChOff | reason: commands need an active session; only an unconnected channel connects | You connect Gmail or Spruce; whoever connects it manages it until practice roles exist (PM-519).
%% event someone else connects the channel | by another physician | needs ChOff | reason: only an unconnected channel connects | Another practice member connects and manages it.
%% event the provider authorizes the channel | by the messaging provider | needs ChConnecting | reason: only a connecting channel is authorized | The channel catches up without duplicates.
%% event the provider refuses the channel | by the messaging provider | needs ChConnecting | reason: only a connecting channel is refused | The channel needs reconnecting.
%% event the provider revokes access or an administrator blocks it | by the messaging provider | needs ChLive | reason: only a live channel loses its grant | Only this needs Reconnect (PM-1275).
%% event reconnect the channel | by you | needs SIn, MgrYes, ChProblem | reason: the manager reconnects a channel that needs it | You reconnect it.
%% event disconnect the channel | by you | needs SIn, MgrYes | reason: only the messaging manager disconnects (PM-519) | Access and in-flight work stop.
%% event the disconnect completes | by the messaging provider | needs ChDisconnecting, MLFree | reason: only a disconnecting channel completes, and it waits out a correction's Undo like everything else touching the conversation (PM:552-559) | Messages never accepted into a record and open reply drafts are deleted; accepted evidence stays under the record's policy.
%% event a message arrives from a known sender | by the messaging channel | needs ChLive, MLNone | reason: only a live channel delivers; known-sender rules link on arrival (PM-190) | The message links to the patient at once.
%% event Coda suggests a patient or is unsure | by Coda | needs MLDeciding | reason: only a message being matched | Matching always ends here when Coda can't tell, so a person decides; how long the runtime tries is not the graph's (Dev 2026-10-24). The message waits to be matched; who sees it on Today is a projection.
%% event Coda finds it is not a patient message | by Coda | needs MLDeciding, MLWaiting | reason: only an unmatched message | It stays out of patient work until the sender writes again.
%% event confirm the match | by you | command on the message match: Confirm, clicked while SIn | needs ADemo, AClin, MLWaiting | reason: only a message waiting to be matched; acting on a patient needs you to see them, at least who they are | Any signed-in physician confirms Coda's suggestion (Dev 2026-10-23); the message becomes the patient's evidence.
%% event confirm another patient | by you | command on the message match: Another patient, clicked while SIn | needs MLWaiting | reason: only a message waiting to be matched | You match it to someone else.
%% event mark the message not a patient | by you | command on the message match: Not a patient, clicked while SIn | needs MLWaiting | reason: only a message waiting to be matched | It stays out of patient work until the sender writes again.
%% event the sender writes again | by the messaging channel | needs ChLive, MLUnlinked | reason: only a live channel delivers | Coda looks at it afresh.
%% event link the message to the patient | by you | command on the message match: Link, clicked while SIn | needs ADemo, AClin, MLUnlinked, MLOther | reason: only an unlinked message or another patient's; acting on a patient needs you to see them, at least who they are | You link it; it becomes the patient's evidence.
%% event the patient writes again | by the patient | needs ChLive, MLLinked | reason: only a live channel delivers to a linked conversation | A newer message in the conversation.
%% event another patient chosen for the message | by you | command on the message match: Move to another patient, clicked while SIn | needs ADemo, AClin, MgrYes, MLLinked | reason: only the messaging manager corrects a linked match (A3, Dev 2026-10-01); acting on a patient needs you to see them, at least who they are | The correction goes forward only, with Undo for a few seconds.
%% event the message is marked not a patient | by you | command on the message match: Mark not a patient, clicked while SIn | needs ADemo, AClin, MgrYes, MLLinked | reason: only the messaging manager corrects a linked match (A3, Dev 2026-10-01); acting on a patient needs you to see them, at least who they are | The correction goes forward only, with Undo for a few seconds.
%% event undo the correction | by you | command on the message match: Undo the correction, clicked while SIn | needs ADemo, AClin, MLUndoOther, MLUndoNot | reason: only while a correction's Undo shows; acting on a patient needs you to see them, at least who they are | The correction is undone and the reply restored exactly (Dev 2026-10-23).
%% event the correction's Undo ends | by the clock | needs MLUndoOther, MLUndoNot | reason: only a correction with Undo showing | This patient's reply work goes; what was built on the message is withheld until the immediate re-review revises, re-authors, ends or closes it (N2, PM:701-711).
%% event Coda can't read a message from the patient | by Coda | A message Coda couldn't read puts the patient on Today, linking to it in Gmail or Spruce; it is never held out of sight (PM-367).
%% event Coda reads the message | by Coda | needs MrCant, MrDone | reason: only an unread message | The mark clears. A part still coming, such as a voicemail transcript, is read again quietly and never shown as unread (patient-messaging.md:378).
%% event mark the unread message done | by you | command on the unread message: Done, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, MrCant | reason: Done needs clinical access and a message Coda couldn't read | You've handled it yourself.
%% event mark no reply needed | by you | command on the reply: No reply needed, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, MRReady, MRNewMsg, MLLinked | reason: only an open reply on the linked message | The reply closes with a brief Undo.
%% event undo no reply needed | by you | command on the reply: Undo no reply needed, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, MRUndo | reason: the reply is clinical content; only while its Undo shows | The reply reopens exactly.
%% event the no-reply Undo ends | by the clock | needs MRUndo | reason: only a reply with Undo showing | The reply is closed.
%% event the practice replies in the channel | by the practice in Gmail or Spruce | needs ChLive, MLLinked | reason: only a live linked conversation | The card shows it at once, as a fact, and the review of that conversation wakes.
%% event edit the reply | by you | needs SIn, AClin, MRReady, MRNewMsg, MLLinked | reason: commands need an active session and clinical access; the reply belongs to the linked message | Your reply box is your private draft; your edits stay yours.
%% event use Coda's update | by you | command on the reply: Use Coda's update, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, RtOffered | reason: the reply is clinical content; only while Coda's update is offered | Coda's newer text replaces yours, with Restore my version.
%% event restore my version | by you | command on the reply: Restore my version, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, RtRestorable | reason: the reply is clinical content; only while your earlier text can be restored | Your earlier text comes back; one restore point.
%% event send the reply | by you | command on the reply: Send, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, MRReady, MRNewMsg, MLLinked, ChLive, WIdle@revision | reason: Coda sends only the exact words you approved, on the linked conversation through a live channel, and not while a revision is rewriting them (PM:160; Copy waits the same way) | Coda sends exactly the text in your reply box through the channel, shown to the patient and the practice as sent by Coda for you (Dev 2026-10-24).
%% event the channel sends the reply | by the messaging provider | needs MRSending, MRSendingNew | reason: only a reply Coda is sending can be sent | The channel reports the reply sent. Delivery and reading are the channel's to report, never assumed from sending (PM:161).
%% event the channel can't send the reply | by the messaging provider | needs MRSending, MRSendingNew | reason: only a reply Coda is sending can fail | The channel refuses or fails; your text stays in the reply box and Send can be tried again.
%% event ask Coda to revise the reply | by you | command on the reply: Ask Coda to revise, clicked while SIn | needs AClin, MRReady, MRNewMsg, MLLinked | reason: only an open reply on the linked message | "Tell Coda what to change": Coda revises your saved reply in place; Copy waits while it runs.
  state "Physician web app" as App {

    %% Practice membership is an input from the practice; roles are not modeled yet.
    state "Practice membership" as Member {
      [*] --> MYes
      [*] --> MNo
      state "A member of the practice" as MYes
      state "Not a member of the practice" as MNo
      MYes --> MNo : practice access removed
      MNo --> MYes : practice access granted
    }
    --
    %% Session expiry is not sign-out (Dev 2026-10-23): a prompt covers the screen and hides patient
    %% content; signing in again returns exactly where the physician was. Everything shown while
    %% signed in is a part of Signed in, so it closes with the session by construction.
    state "Physician session" as Session {
      state "Signed out" as SOut {
        [*] --> SPage
        state "Sign-in page" as SPage
        state "No access to this practice" as SRefused
        SPage --> SRefused : sign in to the practice [not a member]
        %% when MNo | reason: only practice members get in
        SPage --> SRefused : sign in through a link [not a member]
        %% when MNo | reason: only practice members get in
        SRefused --> SPage : try another account
      }
      state "Signed in" as SSession {
        state "Sign-in state" as Auth {
          [*] --> SIn
          state "Signed in to the practice" as SIn
          state "Session expired, sign in to continue" as SExpired
          SIn --> SExpired : the session expires
          SExpired --> SIn : sign in again
        }
        --
        %% Today is the to-do list, the patient page is the relationship, a conversation is one
        %% intentional chat. Navigation never changes patient work (CT-064).
        state "Screen" as Screen {
          [*] --> PToday
          state "Today" as PToday
          state "Patient page" as PPatient {
            %% The source pane, written once: it belongs to the surface that opened it and closes with it.
            %% Another citation on that surface changes only it; how many panes show at once is the app's.
            state "Source pane" as SourceShape {
              %% shape source
              [*] --> EClosed
              state "No source open {where}" as EClosed
              state "Source open {where}" as EOpen {
                [*] --> EPreview
                state "Citation preview {where}" as EPreview
                state "Loading the source {where}" as ELoading
                state "Source text shown {where}" as EShown
                state "Preview kept {where}, source couldn't load, with Retry" as EFailed
                state "Preview only {where}, no qualified source text" as ENoText
                EPreview --> ELoading : expand the source
                ELoading --> EShown : the source loads
                ELoading --> EFailed : the source fails to load
                ELoading --> ENoText : the source has no qualified text
                EFailed --> ELoading : retry the source
              }
              EOpen --> EClosed : close the source
            }
            state "Source pane on the patient page" as EPg {
              %% use source as page: where = on the patient page
              EClosed --> EOpen : open a citation in the patient summary
              EOpen --> EOpen : open a citation in the patient summary
              EClosed --> EOpen : go to a source from Sources
              EOpen --> EOpen : go to a source from Sources
            }
            [*] --> EPg
          }
          state "Conversation" as PConv {
            state "Source pane in the conversation" as ECv {
              %% use source as conversation: where = in the conversation
              EClosed --> EOpen : open a citation in the conversation
              EOpen --> EOpen : open a citation in the conversation
            }
            [*] --> ECv
          }
          state "Patient identity only" as PDemo
          state "That patient is not available" as PGone
          PToday --> PPatient : open the patient [clinical access]
          %% when AClin | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PDemo --> PPatient : open the patient [clinical access]
          %% when AClin | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PGone --> PPatient : open the patient [clinical access]
          %% when AClin | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PToday --> PDemo : open the patient [identity only]
          %% when ADemo | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PGone --> PDemo : open the patient [identity only]
          %% when ADemo | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PToday --> PGone : open the patient [no access]
          %% when ANone | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PToday --> PPatient : follow a link [clinical access]
          %% when AClin | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PPatient --> PPatient : follow a link [clinical access]
          %% when AClin | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PDemo --> PPatient : follow a link [clinical access]
          %% when AClin | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PGone --> PPatient : follow a link [clinical access]
          %% when AClin | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PToday --> PDemo : follow a link [identity only]
          %% when ADemo | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PDemo --> PDemo : follow a link [identity only]
          %% when ADemo | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PGone --> PDemo : follow a link [identity only]
          %% when ADemo | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PToday --> PGone : follow a link [no access]
          %% when ANone | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PPatient --> PGone : follow a link [no access]
          %% when ANone | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PDemo --> PGone : follow a link [no access]
          %% when ANone | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          %% Discuss, and Stop and discuss once accepted, open the work's exact anchored conversation (px.md:133, 514).
          PToday --> PConv : you open a conversation
          PPatient --> PConv : you open a conversation
          PPatient --> PConv : start a new conversation
          PPatient --> PConv : send
          PConv --> PPatient : open the patient [clinical access]
          %% when AClin | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PConv --> PToday : go to Today
          PConv --> PDemo : clinical access reduced
          PConv --> PGone : patient access removed
          PConv --> PPatient : follow a link [clinical access]
          %% when AClin | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PConv --> PDemo : follow a link [identity only]
          %% when ADemo | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PConv --> PGone : follow a link [no access]
          %% when ANone | reason: you land where your access allows; identity only never shows clinical content (CT-012, PX-047)
          PPatient --> PToday : go to Today
          PDemo --> PToday : go to Today
          PGone --> PToday : go to Today
          PPatient --> PDemo : clinical access reduced
          PDemo --> PPatient : clinical access granted
          PPatient --> PGone : patient access removed
          PDemo --> PGone : patient access removed
        }
        --
        %% PX "One shared reader opens everything" over the current page; closing returns exactly. The
        %% reader owns only which item is open and whether it loaded. Notices are read from the item's
        %% owner: a concern revised while you read it is new to you again (change notice, view the
        %% current version by opening it); a briefing whose visit moved or ended is history.
        state "Reader" as Reader {
          [*] --> RNone
          [*] --> RLink : sign in through a link
          state "No reader open" as RNone
          state "Following a link" as RLink
          state "Reader open" as ROpen {
            state "What is open" as RItem {
              [*] --> RConcern
              state "Reading the concern" as RConcern
              state "Reading the briefing" as RBriefing
              state "Reading the follow-up" as RFollow
              state "Reading past work" as RPast
              RFollow --> RPast : open past work from the follow-up
              RConcern --> RPast : open the work that raised the concern
            }
            --
            state "Source pane in the reader" as ERd {
              %% use source as reader: where = in the reader
              EClosed --> EOpen : open a citation in the reader
              EOpen --> EOpen : open a citation in the reader
            }
            --
            state "Reading load" as RLoad {
              %% use read as reading: read = the reading
              RdShown --> RdLoading : open past work from the follow-up
              RdKept --> RdLoading : open past work from the follow-up
              RdFailed --> RdLoading : open past work from the follow-up
              RdShown --> RdLoading : open the work that raised the concern
              RdKept --> RdLoading : open the work that raised the concern
              RdFailed --> RdLoading : open the work that raised the concern
            }
          }
          RNone --> RConcern : open the concern
          ROpen --> RConcern : open the concern
          RNone --> RBriefing : open the briefing
          ROpen --> RBriefing : open the briefing
          RNone --> RFollow : open the follow-up
          ROpen --> RFollow : open the follow-up
          RNone --> RPast : open past work
          ROpen --> RPast : open past work
          RNone --> RLink : follow a link
          ROpen --> RLink : follow a link
          RLink --> RConcern : the link opens the concern
          RLink --> RBriefing : the link opens the briefing
          RLink --> RFollow : the link opens the follow-up
          RLink --> RPast : the link opens past work
          RLink --> RNone : the link shows the patient page
          ROpen --> RNone : close the reader
          ROpen --> RNone : discuss what you're reading
          ROpen --> RNone : stop and discuss the {held}
          ROpen --> RNone : stop and discuss the follow-up
          RConcern --> RNone : mark the concern done
          ROpen --> RNone : go to Today
          ROpen --> RNone : open the patient
          ROpen --> RNone : access to the patient narrows
          RLink --> RNone : access to the patient narrows
          %% never ClinicalReaderNeedsAccess: Reader open & Identity only -- Clinical content never shows without clinical access.
          %% never ClinicalReaderNeedsAnyAccess: Reader open & Cannot see the patient -- Clinical content never shows without access to the patient.
        }
        --
        %% PX "Updates is the day's log": the record of everything Coda did that the physician never
        %% maintains (Dev 2026-10-23). Rows, groups ("Reviewed, nothing for you"), counts and change
        %% marks are projections from the owners; the panel owns only what is open and the day's read.
        state "Updates panel" as Updates {
          [*] --> UClosed
          state "Updates closed" as UClosed
          state "Updates open" as UOpen {
            state "Updates view" as UView {
              [*] --> UList
              state "Updates list" as UList
              state "Reading an update" as UReading {
                [*] --> UpdRead
                state "Update read" as UpdRead {
                  %% use read as update: read = the update
                }
              }
              UList --> UReading : open an update
              UReading --> UReading : another update opens
              UReading --> UList : back to Updates
              UReading --> UList : access to the patient narrows
            }
            --
            state "Source pane in Updates" as EUp {
              %% use source as updates: where = in Updates
              EClosed --> EOpen : open a citation in Updates
              EOpen --> EOpen : open a citation in Updates
              EOpen --> EClosed : back to Updates
              EOpen --> EClosed : access to the patient narrows
            }
            --
            state "Updates day read" as UDay {
              %% use read as day: read = the Updates day
              RdShown --> RdLoading : you change the Updates day
              RdKept --> RdLoading : you change the Updates day
              RdFailed --> RdLoading : return to today's updates
              RdFailed --> RdLoading : midnight passes [showing today]
              %% when UwToday | reason: an earlier day stays as you chose it
            }
            --
            %% Opening Updates shows today; Earlier steps back and Today returns (px.md:437).
            state "Which day" as UWhen {
              [*] --> UwToday
              state "Showing today" as UwToday
              state "Showing an earlier day" as UwEarlier
              UwToday --> UwEarlier : go to an earlier day
              UwEarlier --> UwEarlier : go to an earlier day
              UwEarlier --> UwToday : return to today's updates
            }
          }
          UClosed --> UOpen : open Updates
          UClosed --> UOpen : open all updates
          UClosed --> UReading : open an update
          UOpen --> UClosed : close Updates
          %% never NoUpdateReadWithoutAccess: Reading an update & Cannot see the patient -- An update about a patient never shows without access to that patient.
          %% never NoUpdateReadWithIdentityOnly: Reading an update & Identity only -- An update's clinical content never shows with identity access only.
        }
        --
        %% Today's list read. Rows and the count are projections from the owners: work in hand you'd
        %% recognise with Stop (px.md:579-585), questions Coda asked you, concerns, can't-restart rows,
        %% messages to match. Today shows only what needs you (Dev 2026-10-23).
        %% How every read behaves, written once. A saved copy shows at once; loading shows only when
        %% nothing can; a refresh is quiet; a failure keeps what is shown with one quiet line and Retry,
        %% and with nothing shown says it couldn't load. A late or empty answer never replaces what is
        %% shown (px.md:438-441, 990; RP-217; the Claude desktop comparison). Each use says when it reads.
        state "Read" as ReadShape {
          %% shape read
          [*] --> RdLoading
          %% except conversation, search
          state "Loading {read}" as RdLoading
          state "Showing {read}" as RdShown
          state "Showing {read}, with one quiet line and Retry" as RdKept
          state "Couldn't load {read}, with Retry" as RdFailed
          RdLoading --> RdShown : {read} shows a saved copy
          RdLoading --> RdShown : {read} loads
          RdShown --> RdShown : {read} loads
          RdKept --> RdShown : {read} loads
          RdLoading --> RdKept : {read} loads in part
          RdShown --> RdKept : {read} loads in part
          RdLoading --> RdFailed : {read} fails to load
          RdShown --> RdKept : {read} fails to load
          RdKept --> RdKept : retry {read}
          RdFailed --> RdLoading : retry {read}
        }
        state "Today list read" as TodayRead {
          %% use read as today: read = Today
          RdFailed --> RdLoading : midnight passes
        }
        --
        %% An existing conversation and its saved draft arrive in one read; a new one has nothing to read.
        state "Conversation read" as ConvRead {
          %% use read as conversation: read = the conversation
          [*] --> CrNone
          state "No conversation to read" as CrNone
          CrNone --> RdLoading : you open a conversation
          RdLoading --> RdLoading : you open a conversation
          RdShown --> RdLoading : you open a conversation
          RdKept --> RdLoading : you open a conversation
          RdFailed --> RdLoading : you open a conversation
          RdLoading --> CrNone : you leave the conversation
          RdShown --> CrNone : you leave the conversation
          RdKept --> CrNone : you leave the conversation
          RdFailed --> CrNone : you leave the conversation
        }
        --
        %% The schedule rail reads on its own; the list never waits on it (px.md:610-616).
        state "Schedule read" as ScheduleRead {
          %% use read as schedule: read = the schedule
          state "No calendar, no schedule area" as ScOff
          RdLoading --> ScOff : the schedule finds no calendar
          RdShown --> ScOff : the schedule finds no calendar
          RdKept --> ScOff : the schedule finds no calendar
          RdFailed --> ScOff : the schedule finds no calendar
          ScOff --> RdLoading : the practice connects a calendar
          RdFailed --> RdLoading : midnight passes
        }
        --
        %% PX "Find patient": one server-side roster search; every roster patient stays
        %% reachable (PX-89, Dev 2026-10-23). How results page is the app's.
        state "Find patient" as Search {
          [*] --> FClosed
          state "Search closed" as FClosed
          state "Search open" as FOpen {
            [*] --> SearchRead
            state "Search read" as SearchRead {
              %% use read as search: read = the search
              [*] --> FIdle
              state "Type to search" as FIdle
              FIdle --> RdLoading : type in find patient
              RdShown --> RdLoading : type in find patient
              RdKept --> RdLoading : type in find patient
              RdFailed --> RdLoading : type in find patient
            }
          }
          FClosed --> FOpen : open find patient
          FOpen --> FClosed : open the patient
          FOpen --> FClosed : close find patient
        }
        --
        %% Decision 8 and Dev 2026-10-24: one receipt per item; a command changes its item only when accepted,
        %% and is refused when the item no longer allows it. A pending command survives expiry and ends at sign-out.
        state "Your command on the {work}" as WorkRc {
          %% template
          %% instance understanding: work = initial understanding
          %% instance review: work = patient review
          %% instance followup: work = follow-up review
          %% instance weekly: work = weekly review
          %% instance prep: work = visit preparation
          %% instance asked: work = asked reply
          %% instance proactive: work = proactive work
          %% instance answer: work = answer
          %% instance revision: work = reply revision
          %% receipt the {work}
        }
        --
        state "Your command on the follow-up" as FollowupRc {
          %% receipt the follow-up
        }
        --
        %% Dictation (px.md:324-356): one tab session owns recording, cancellation and insertion. Leaving the
        %% composer cancels it, and so does expiry (N5): nothing records behind the sign-in prompt.
        state "Dictation" as Dictation {
          [*] --> MicIdle
          state "Microphone idle" as MicIdle
          state "Waiting for microphone permission" as MicAsking
          state "Recording" as MicRecording
          state "Transcribing" as MicTranscribing
          state "Transcript waiting to insert at your cursor" as MicPreview
          state "Dictation failed, your text kept" as MicFailed
          MicIdle --> MicAsking : start dictation [a composer is open]
          %% when PConv, PPatient | reason: only a chat composer takes dictation here; patient search keeps its own control
          MicFailed --> MicAsking : start dictation [a composer is open]
          %% when PConv, PPatient | reason: only a chat composer takes dictation here; patient search keeps its own control
          MicAsking --> MicRecording : the microphone is allowed
          MicAsking --> MicFailed : the microphone is refused
          MicAsking --> MicIdle : release before permission
          MicRecording --> MicTranscribing : stop recording
          MicTranscribing --> MicIdle : the transcript is inserted
          MicTranscribing --> MicPreview : the transcript arrives for a changed target
          MicPreview --> MicIdle : insert the transcript
          MicTranscribing --> MicFailed : transcription fails
          MicAsking --> MicIdle : cancel dictation
          MicRecording --> MicIdle : cancel dictation
          MicTranscribing --> MicIdle : cancel dictation
          MicPreview --> MicIdle : cancel dictation
          MicAsking --> MicIdle : you leave the composer
          MicRecording --> MicIdle : you leave the composer
          MicTranscribing --> MicIdle : you leave the composer
          MicPreview --> MicIdle : you leave the composer
          MicFailed --> MicIdle : you leave the composer
        }
        --
        state "Your command on the concern" as ConcernRc {
          %% receipt the concern
        }
        --
        state "Your command on the conversation" as ConvRc {
          %% receipt the conversation
        }
        --
        %% Conversation archived · Undo shows only after the archive is accepted (px.md:386).
        state "Archive notice" as ArNotice {
          [*] --> ArNone
          state "No archive notice" as ArNone
          state "Conversation archived, with Undo" as ArShown
          ArNone --> ArShown : archive the conversation
          ArShown --> ArShown : archive the conversation
          ArShown --> ArNone : undo the archive
          ArShown --> ArNone : restore the conversation
          ArShown --> ArNone : the archive notice closes
        }
        --
        %% The details form is on this screen only: closing keeps the rating and discards unsaved
        %% edits; a refused save keeps your text (px.md:752-758).
        state "Feedback form" as FbForm {
          [*] --> FmClosed
          state "Feedback details closed" as FmClosed
          state "Feedback details open" as FmOpen {
            [*] --> FmClean
            state "Showing the saved details" as FmClean
            state "Your unsaved reasons or note" as FmEdited
            FmClean --> FmEdited : edit the feedback details
            FmEdited --> FmEdited : edit the feedback details
            FmEdited --> FmClean : save the feedback details
            FmEdited --> FmClean : rate the message up [flipping the rating]
            %% when FbDown | reason: a new rating starts with empty details
            FmEdited --> FmClean : rate the message down [flipping the rating]
            %% when FbUp | reason: a new rating starts with empty details
          }
          FmClosed --> FmOpen : rate the message up
          FmClosed --> FmOpen : rate the message down
          FmOpen --> FmClosed : close the feedback form
          FmOpen --> FmClosed : access to the patient narrows
        }
        --
        %% Rating and details save one at a time; an uncertain save checks its receipt before retry.
        state "Your command on the feedback" as FeedbackRc {
          %% receipt the feedback
        }
        --
        state "Your command on the queued messages" as QueueRc {
          %% receipt the queued messages
        }
        --
        state "Your command on the patient's connection" as ConnRc {
          %% receipt the patient's connection
        }
        --
        state "Your command on the message match" as MatchRc {
          %% receipt the message match
        }
        --
        state "Your command on the unread message" as UnreadRc {
          %% receipt the unread message
        }
        --
        state "Your command on the reply" as ReplyRc {
          %% receipt the reply
        }
      }
      [*] --> SOut
      SOut --> SSession : sign in to the practice [member]
      %% when MYes | reason: only practice members get in
      SOut --> PPatient : sign in through a link [clinical access]
      %% when MYes, AClin | reason: only practice members get in
      SOut --> PDemo : sign in through a link [identity only]
      %% when MYes, ADemo | reason: only practice members get in
      SOut --> PGone : sign in through a link [no access]
      %% when MYes, ANone | reason: only practice members get in
      SSession --> SSession : a different physician signs in
      SExpired --> SOut : reopen Coda after the session ended
      SSession --> SOut : sign out
      SSession --> SOut : practice access removed
    }
    --
    %% CT-012, PX-047: roster access and clinical access are separate; identity-only access shows
    %% the source identity and nothing clinical. Access results are inputs.
    state "Access to the patient" as Access {
      [*] --> ANone
      [*] --> ADemo
      [*] --> AClin
      state "Cannot see the patient" as ANone
      state "Identity only" as ADemo
      state "Clinical access" as AClin
      ANone --> ADemo : identity access granted
      ANone --> AClin : clinical access granted
      ADemo --> AClin : clinical access granted
      AClin --> ADemo : clinical access reduced
      AClin --> ANone : patient access removed
      ADemo --> ANone : patient access removed
    }
    --
    %% CT clinical responsibilities: a review follows only when something new arrives; how often sources
    %% are checked is the runtime's (infrastructure-gaps.md). PX "Records as of" keeps the last good pull
    %% and names a failure. Coda keeps working from the last good records while the source is unavailable (Dev
    %% 2026-10-23). The outage lines are projections from this owner.
    state "Records source" as Source {
      [*] --> SrcConnecting
      state "Connecting the source" as SrcConnecting
      state "Records kept" as SrcHave {
        [*] --> SrcCurrent
        state "Records current" as SrcCurrent
        state "Records couldn't be updated" as SrcFailed
        %% A source that comes back has not updated yet: its records stay as of the last good update
        %% until it does, so nothing claims they are current early (Astra review of #148).
        state "Source back, records as of the last good update" as SrcBack
        SrcCurrent --> SrcFailed : the records source can't update
        SrcBack --> SrcFailed : the records source can't update
        SrcFailed --> SrcCurrent : the records source updates again
        SrcBack --> SrcCurrent : the records source updates again
        SrcFailed --> SrcCurrent : new records arrive
        SrcBack --> SrcCurrent : new records arrive
      }
      state "Source unavailable, last good records kept" as SrcGoneKept
      state "Source unavailable, no records yet" as SrcGoneEmpty
      SrcConnecting --> SrcCurrent : new records arrive
      SrcConnecting --> SrcGoneEmpty : the source becomes unavailable
      SrcHave --> SrcGoneKept : the source becomes unavailable
      SrcGoneEmpty --> SrcConnecting : the source is reconnected
      SrcGoneKept --> SrcBack : the source is reconnected
      SrcConnecting --> SrcGoneEmpty : the practice's records source goes down
      SrcHave --> SrcGoneKept : the practice's records source goes down
      SrcGoneEmpty --> SrcConnecting : the practice's records source comes back
      SrcGoneKept --> SrcBack : the practice's records source comes back
    }
    --
    %% Decision 9 (Dev 2026-10-23, practice-wide line approved 2026-10-24): when the practice's whole
    %% source is down, Today carries one line for the practice, never a row per patient. This owner
    %% holds the practice-wide fact; each patient's records owner holds that patient's last good pull.
    state "Practice records source" as PSource {
      [*] --> PsUp
      state "Practice source up" as PsUp
      state "Practice source down, one line on Today" as PsDown
      PsUp --> PsDown : the practice's records source goes down
      PsDown --> PsUp : the practice's records source comes back
      %% never NoCurrentRecordsWhileDown: Practice source down, one line on Today & Records kept -- While the practice's whole source is down, no patient's records read as current.
    }
    --
    %% Connection lifecycle (Dev 2026-10-22/23), practice side only: one owner for the patient's connection,
    %% invitation included. The roster shows status without notifications. Connected means sharing;
    %% there is no pause (Dev 2026-10-23). An ended connection can be invited again; consent wording is
    %% fixed for the MVP, so there is no re-consent state.
    state "Practice connection" as Connection {
      [*] --> PcNone
      state "Not connected" as PcNone
      state "Invited" as PcInvited {
        [*] --> PcSending
        state "Sending the invitation" as PcSending
        state "Invitation sent" as PcSent {
          [*] --> PcFresh
          state "No reminder yet" as PcFresh
          state "Reminder sent" as PcReminded
          PcFresh --> PcReminded : the invitation reminder goes out
        }
        state "Invitation couldn't be delivered, with Resend" as PcUndelivered
        PcSending --> PcSent : the invitation is delivered
        PcSending --> PcUndelivered : the invitation can't be delivered
        PcUndelivered --> PcSending : resend the invitation
        PcSent --> PcSending : resend the invitation
      }
      state "Connected" as PcConnected
      state "Connection ended" as PcEnded {
        [*] --> PcLeft
        state "Ended, the patient left" as PcLeft
        state "Ended, discharged by the practice" as PcDischarged
        state "Ended, the patient's account was deleted" as PcDeleted
      }
      PcNone --> PcInvited : invite the patient
      PcEnded --> PcInvited : invite the patient
      PcInvited --> PcConnected : the patient joins and consents
      PcInvited --> PcNone : cancel the invitation
      PcReminded --> PcNone : the invitation expires
      PcInvited --> PcNone : the patient's account is deleted
      PcConnected --> PcLeft : the patient leaves the practice
      PcConnected --> PcDischarged : discharge the patient
      PcConnected --> PcDeleted : the patient's account is deleted
      PcConnected --> PcConnected : a shared Duet record arrives
      PcConnected --> PcConnected : the patient sends For my doctor
      PcConnected --> PcConnected : the practice's visit reaches the patient's Duet
    }
    --
    %% The patient summary is what initial understanding writes; later work builds on it.
    state "Initial understanding" as Summary {
      [*] --> SumNone
      state "Initial understanding not finished" as SumNone
      state "Initial understanding finished" as SumWritten
      SumNone --> SumWritten : Coda finishes the initial understanding
    }
    --
    %% One lifecycle for every kind of work. The kinds are examples, not a menu: proactive work is
    %% whatever Coda takes on itself, with the same outcomes and limits.
    state "Coda's work: {work}" as Work {
      %% template
      %% Instance values say what each kind allows: {held} kinds can be stopped (initial
      %% understanding cannot, CT-014), {left} kinds leave a Today row when Coda can't restart them,
      %% and the {fresh} (a given chat answer) offers one tap to update when newer records arrive.
      %% {row} kinds have a row on Today when Coda can't restart them.
      %% instance understanding: work = initial understanding
      %% instance review: work = patient review, held = patient review, left = patient review, row = patient review
      %% instance followup: work = follow-up review, row = follow-up review
      %% instance weekly: work = weekly review, held = weekly review
      %% instance prep: work = visit preparation, held = visit preparation, left = visit preparation, row = visit preparation
      %% instance asked: work = asked reply, held = asked reply, left = asked reply, row = asked reply
      %% instance proactive: work = proactive work, held = proactive work
      %% instance answer: work = answer, held = answer, fresh = answer
      %% instance revision: work = reply revision, held = reply revision
      %% Idle, or in hand. Work in hand is active (owed or running) or stalled (waiting
      %% for an opportunity, or failed with Try again; a question for you is a finish, never a wait, CT:671). Stop, and anything that
      %% ends the work's occasion, takes work in hand back to idle wherever it is.
      state "{work}: lifecycle" as Life {
        [*] --> WIdle
        state "{work} not in hand" as WIdle {
          [*] --> WNone
          state "No {work} owed" as WNone
          %% A given answer is what was said: it keeps the records it used, marked when newer ones
          %% arrive (Dev 2026-10-26, live where you work; history as it was).
          state "{work} given" as WGiven
          %% only answer
          state "{work} given, newer records since, with Update" as WDoneStale
          %% only answer
          WGiven --> WDoneStale : news for the patient
          %% only answer
        }
        state "{work} in hand" as WHand {
          [*] --> WActive
          state "{work} active" as WActive {
            [*] --> WOwed
            state "{work} owed, waiting to start" as WOwed
            state "Coda is working on the {work}" as WRun
          }
          state "{work} stalled" as WStalled {
            [*] --> WWait
            state "{work} waiting for the next opportunity, with Try again" as WWait
            state "{work} couldn't finish, with Try again" as WFail
          }
        }
        WIdle --> WOwed : news for the patient [initial understanding not finished]
        %% when SumNone | reason: until the initial understanding finishes, news goes into it rather than a patient review
        %% only understanding
        WStalled --> WOwed : news for the patient [initial understanding not finished]
        %% when SumNone | reason: until the initial understanding finishes, news goes into it rather than a patient review
        %% only understanding
        WIdle --> WOwed : you write to Coda [initial understanding not finished] / may try the initial understanding again
        %% when SumNone | reason: explicit physician direction may wake another attempt (CT-1196)
        %% only understanding
        WStalled --> WOwed : you write to Coda [initial understanding not finished] / may try the initial understanding again
        %% when SumNone | reason: explicit physician direction may wake another attempt (CT-1196)
        %% only understanding
        WIdle --> WOwed : news for the patient [initial understanding finished]
        %% when SumWritten | reason: after the initial understanding, news starts a patient review
        %% only review
        WStalled --> WOwed : news for the patient [initial understanding finished]
        %% when SumWritten | reason: after the initial understanding, news starts a patient review
        %% only review
        WIdle --> WOwed : the follow-up comes due
        %% only followup
        WIdle --> WOwed : review the follow-up now
        %% only followup
        WStalled --> WOwed : the follow-up comes due
        %% only followup
        WIdle --> WOwed : the weekly cycle comes round [not held]
        %% when not HYes | reason: a stopped weekly review stays held; later cycles don't release it (CT:110)
        %% only weekly
        WStalled --> WOwed : the weekly cycle comes round [not held]
        %% when not HYes | reason: a stopped weekly review stays held; later cycles don't release it (CT:110)
        %% only weekly
        WIdle --> WOwed : the visit comes into preparation range
        %% only prep
        WIdle --> WOwed : ask Coda to reply
        %% only asked
        WStalled --> WOwed : ask Coda to reply
        %% only asked
        WIdle --> WOwed : Coda decides to take something on
        %% only proactive
        WStalled --> WOwed : Coda decides to take something on
        %% only proactive
        WOwed --> WRun : Coda starts the {work} [records kept]
        %% when SrcHave, SrcGoneKept | reason: Coda reads only authorized evidence it has (N1)
        %% only understanding
        WOwed --> WRun : Coda starts the {work} [Duet shared records]
        %% when PcConnected, PcEnded | reason: Coda reads only authorized evidence it has (N1)
        %% only understanding
        WOwed --> WRun : Coda starts the {work}
        %% only answer, revision
        WOwed --> WRun : Coda starts the {work} [no patient review running]
        %% when WIdle@review, WOwed@review, WStalled@review | reason: an ask waits behind a patient review already running (px.md:167)
        %% only asked
        WOwed --> WRun : Coda starts the {work} [initial understanding finished]
        %% when SumWritten | reason: later work builds on the initial understanding (N13, RP:810-811); work for one patient otherwise runs side by side (Dev 2026-10-24)
        %% only review, followup, weekly, prep, proactive
        WRun --> WFail : the {work} fails
        WRun --> WWait : Coda waits on the {work} for missing information
        WFail --> WOwed : try the {work} again
        WWait --> WOwed : try the {work} again
        WOwed --> WIdle : Coda can't restart the {work}
        WFail --> WIdle : Coda can't restart the {work}
        WRun --> WIdle : Coda finishes the {work}
        %% except answer
        WRun --> WGiven : Coda finishes the {work}
        %% only answer
        WRun --> WOwed : the correction's Undo ends
        %% except asked, revision
        WHand --> WIdle : you stop the {held}
        %% except understanding, followup
        WHand --> WIdle : you stop the follow-up
        %% only followup
        WIdle --> WOwed : resume the {held} [held]
        %% when HYes | reason: only held work resumes
        %% except understanding, followup
        WStalled --> WOwed : resume the {held} [held]
        %% when HYes | reason: only held work resumes
        %% except understanding, followup
        WIdle --> WOwed : resume the follow-up [the follow-up held]
        %% when FHeld | reason: only a held follow-up resumes its review
        %% only followup
        WDoneStale --> WOwed : update the {fresh} with the newer records
        %% only answer
        WHand --> WIdle : cancel the follow-up
        %% only followup
        WHand --> WIdle : complete the follow-up
        %% only followup
        WHand --> WIdle : change the follow-up
        %% only followup
        WIdle --> WOwed : message news
        %% only review
        WStalled --> WOwed : message news
        %% only review
        WIdle --> WOwed : ask Coda to revise the reply
        %% only revision
        WStalled --> WOwed : ask Coda to revise the reply
        %% only revision
        WHand --> WIdle : the correction's Undo ends
        %% only asked, revision
        WHand --> WIdle : the disconnect completes
        %% only asked, revision
        WHand --> WIdle : mark no reply needed
        %% only asked, revision
        WHand --> WIdle : Coda finishes the patient review [a linked message, no reply open] / may propose a reply
        %% when MLLinked, MRNone | reason: a reply the review proposes first answers the ask (px.md:167)
        %% only asked
        WHand --> WIdle : Coda finishes the patient review [the practice replied] / may close the reply as answered
        %% when PrShown, MRReady, MRNewMsg | reason: the reply closes as answered only while open and after the practice replied
        %% only revision
        WIdle --> WOwed : you write to Coda
        %% only answer
        WStalled --> WOwed : you write to Coda
        %% only answer
        WIdle --> WOwed : the queued message starts
        %% only answer
        WStalled --> WOwed : the queued message starts
        %% only answer
        WHand --> WIdle : you lose clinical access
        %% only asked, answer, revision
        WHand --> WIdle : the visit is cancelled
        %% only prep
        WHand --> WIdle : the visit is moved
        %% only prep
        WOwed --> WIdle : the visit ends
        %% only prep
        WStalled --> WIdle : the visit ends
        %% only prep
      }
      --
      %% Whatever Coda is working on, it takes in what arrives meanwhile before it finishes, so nothing
      %% it publishes rests on an older reading (Dev 2026-10-26). Responding to news stays the patient
      %% review's (or the initial understanding's, before one exists). How the runtime notices and
      %% re-reads is not the graph's (Dev 2026-10-24). Each start reads afresh, so starting clears it.
      state "{work}: news while working" as News {
        [*] --> NwNone
        state "Nothing new since it started" as NwNone
        state "Something new arrived since it started" as NwSeen
        NwNone --> NwSeen : news for the patient [working]
        %% when WRun | reason: only news that arrives while the work runs is news it missed
        NwSeen --> NwNone : Coda starts the {work}
        NwSeen --> NwNone : Coda takes in what arrived in the {work}
      }
      --
      %% Stop holds the work with Resume where it was stopped. New causes still make new work owed;
      %% for the weekly review alone, a stop also holds later cycles. A follow-up's hold is the
      %% follow-up's own (Stopped, held until Resume), so its review keeps no second one.
      state "{work}: held by you" as Hold {
        %% except understanding, followup
        [*] --> HNo
        state "Not held" as HNo
        state "Held with Resume" as HYes
        %% except understanding, followup
        HNo --> HYes : you stop the {held} [work in hand]
        %% when WHand | reason: only work in hand can be held
        %% except understanding
        HYes --> HNo : resume the {held}
        %% except understanding
        HYes --> HNo : you write to Coda
        %% only answer
        HNo --> HYes : you lose clinical access [work in hand]
        %% when WHand | reason: losing access stops what this physician started
        %% only asked, answer, revision
        HYes --> HNo : the correction's Undo ends
        %% only asked, revision
        HYes --> HNo : the disconnect completes
        %% only asked, revision
        HYes --> HNo : mark no reply needed
        %% only asked, revision
        HYes --> HNo : send the reply
        %% only asked, revision
        HYes --> HNo : Coda finishes the patient review [a linked message, no reply open] / may propose a reply
        %% when MLLinked, MRNone | reason: a reply the review proposes first answers the ask (px.md:167)
        %% only asked
        HYes --> HNo : Coda finishes the patient review [the practice replied] / may close the reply as answered
        %% when PrShown, MRReady, MRNewMsg | reason: the reply closes as answered only while open and after the practice replied
        %% only revision
        HYes --> HNo : the visit is cancelled
        %% only prep
        HYes --> HNo : the visit is moved
        %% only prep
        HYes --> HNo : the visit ends
        %% only prep
      }
      --
      %% R6: what a can't-restart run left waits on Today with Done, and rides the next run.
      state "{work}: left for you" as Left {
        %% only review, followup, prep, asked
        [*] --> LNone
        state "Nothing left for you" as LNone
        state "Coda couldn't restart; what's left is on Today with Done" as LShown {
          %% only review, followup, prep, asked
          [*] --> LNew
          state "New to you" as LNew
          state "Opened by you" as LOpened
          LNew --> LOpened : open the {row} that couldn't restart
          LOpened --> LNew : Coda can't restart the {work}
        }
        LNone --> LShown : Coda can't restart the {work}
        %% only review, followup, prep, asked
        LShown --> LNone : mark the {left} done
        %% only review, prep, asked
        LShown --> LNone : complete the follow-up
        %% only followup
        LShown --> LNone : change the follow-up
        %% only followup
        LShown --> LNone : cancel the follow-up
        %% only followup
        LShown --> LNone : Coda finishes the {work}
        %% only review, followup, prep, asked
        LShown --> LNone : the visit is cancelled
        %% only prep
        LShown --> LNone : the visit is moved
        %% only prep
        LShown --> LNone : the visit ends
        %% only prep
      }
    }
    --
    %% CT visibility: a concern is what Coda thinks needs a physician. Any work may raise, revise or
    %% close one when it finishes; a revision is new again to everyone. Opening is personal; Done is
    %% shared. Urgency belongs to the concern (bug 8) and exists only while it needs attention.
    %% Coda never retires an urgent concern nobody has opened (RP-289).
    state "Concern" as Concern {
      [*] --> CRest
      state "No concern needs you" as CRest {
        [*] --> CNone
        state "No concern" as CNone
        state "Marked done" as CDone
        state "Closed by Coda" as CClosed
      }
      state "Needs attention" as CNeeds {
        state "Who has opened it" as Opening {
          [*] --> CUnopened
          state "Not yet opened by you" as CUnopened
          state "Seen by another physician, still new to you" as COtherOpened
          state "Opened by you" as COpened
          CUnopened --> COpened : the concern is shown
          COtherOpened --> COpened : the concern is shown
          CUnopened --> COtherOpened : another physician opens the concern
          COtherOpened --> CUnopened : Coda finishes any work with an update for you / may revise the concern
          COpened --> CUnopened : Coda finishes any work with an update for you / may revise the concern
          COtherOpened --> CUnopened : Coda finishes any work with an update for you [not already now] / may raise the urgency
          %% when UrgToday, UrgLowered | reason: a raise to now makes the concern new to everyone (RP:286)
          COpened --> CUnopened : Coda finishes any work with an update for you [not already now] / may raise the urgency
          %% when UrgToday, UrgLowered | reason: a raise to now makes the concern new to everyone (RP:286)
        }
        --
        state "Urgency" as Urgency {
          [*] --> UrgToday
          state "For today" as UrgToday
          state "Needs you now" as UrgNow
          state "For today, lowered from now before anyone opened it" as UrgLowered
          UrgToday --> UrgNow : Coda finishes any work with an update for you / may raise the urgency
          UrgLowered --> UrgNow : Coda finishes any work with an update for you / may raise the urgency
          UrgNow --> UrgToday : Coda finishes any work with an update for you [opened since marked now] / may lower the urgency
          %% when COpened, COtherOpened | reason: a demotion keeps the now mark until a physician opens it (RP:286-289)
          UrgNow --> UrgLowered : Coda finishes any work with an update for you [nobody opened it at now] / may lower the urgency
          %% when CUnopened | reason: a demotion keeps the now mark until a physician opens it (RP:286-289)
          UrgLowered --> UrgToday : the concern is shown
          UrgLowered --> UrgToday : another physician opens the concern
        }
        --
        state "Visit link" as Link {
          [*] --> NgNo
          state "Not tied to a visit" as NgNo
          state "Tied to the upcoming visit" as NgVisit
          state "Its visit passed while it was marked now and unopened; ends when anyone opens it" as NgPassed
          state "About a patient message; stays with its message" as NgMsg
          NgMsg --> NgNo : Coda finishes the patient review with an update for you [the message is no longer linked] / re-authors the concern from the patient's own record
          %% when not MLLinked | reason: a message no longer linked to this patient, whether moved, marked not a patient or being matched again, is not its evidence, so the re-review decides its concern (N2)
          NgNo --> NgVisit : Coda finishes any work with an update for you [a visit ahead] / may tie the concern to the upcoming visit
          %% when VAhead | reason: only a visit still ahead can be linked to (A7)
          NgVisit --> NgPassed : the visit ends [unopened and marked now]
          %% when CUnopened, UrgNow, UrgLowered | reason: Coda never retires a now mark nobody opened (RP-289)
          NgVisit --> NgPassed : the visit is cancelled [unopened and marked now]
          %% when CUnopened, UrgNow, UrgLowered | reason: Coda never retires a now mark nobody opened (RP-289)
        }
      }
      CRest --> CNeeds : Coda finishes any work with an update for you / may raise a concern
      CRest --> UrgNow : Coda finishes any work with an update for you / may raise an urgent concern
      CRest --> NgVisit : Coda finishes any work with an update for you [a visit ahead] / may raise a nudge for the upcoming visit
      %% when VAhead | reason: only a visit still ahead can be linked to (A7)
      CRest --> NgMsg : Coda finishes the patient review with an update for you [a linked message] / may raise a concern about the message
      %% when MLLinked | reason: only a message linked to this patient is this patient's evidence (PM-500)
      CRest --> NgMsg : Coda finishes the asked reply with an update for you [a linked message] / may raise a concern about the message
      %% when MLLinked | reason: only a message linked to this patient is this patient's evidence (PM-500)
      NgVisit --> CClosed : the visit ends [opened]
      %% when COpened, COtherOpened | reason: an opened visit nudge ends with its visit
      NgVisit --> CClosed : the visit ends [unopened, for today]
      %% when CUnopened, UrgToday | reason: an unopened nudge for today ends with its visit; one marked now waits to be opened (RP-289)
      NgVisit --> CClosed : the visit is cancelled [opened]
      %% when COpened, COtherOpened | reason: an opened visit nudge ends with its visit
      NgVisit --> CClosed : the visit is cancelled [unopened, for today]
      %% when CUnopened, UrgToday | reason: an unopened nudge for today ends with its visit; one marked now waits to be opened (RP-289)
      NgMsg --> CClosed : Coda finishes the patient review with an update for you [the message is no longer linked] / may close the concern
      %% when not MLLinked | reason: a message no longer linked to this patient, whether moved, marked not a patient or being matched again, is not its evidence, so the re-review decides its concern (N2)
      NgMsg --> CClosed : Coda finishes the patient review quietly [the message is no longer linked] / closes the concern
      %% when not MLLinked | reason: a re-review that writes nothing can't re-author a concern, so it closes one whose message is no longer this patient's evidence (N2)
      NgPassed --> CClosed : the concern is shown
      NgPassed --> CClosed : another physician opens the concern
      CNeeds --> CDone : mark the concern done
      CNeeds --> CDone : another physician marks the concern done
      COpened --> CClosed : Coda finishes any work / may close the concern
      COtherOpened --> CClosed : Coda finishes any work / may close the concern
      CUnopened --> CClosed : Coda finishes any work [unopened, for today] / may close the concern
      %% when UrgToday | reason: Coda never retires an urgent concern nobody has opened (RP-289)
    }
    --
    %% CT unified follow-up contract: the one forward-looking responsibility. You create, change, stop,
    %% resume and cancel it directly. Any work may create or revise one (A5); a cancel is
    %% respected until new information arrives. A due follow-up stays due until its own review
    %% disposes of it (RP-830), so other work completes it only while that review is not active (X1).
    %% One Stop holds the follow-up and its review together; Resume reviews the current version (M1).
    state "Follow-up" as Followup {
      [*] --> FNone
      state "No follow-up" as FNone
      state "Active follow-up" as FActive {
        [*] --> FWaiting
        state "Not yet due" as FWaiting
        state "Due, its review owed" as FDue
        FWaiting --> FDue : the follow-up comes due
        FDue --> FWaiting : change the follow-up
      }
      state "Stopped, held until Resume" as FHeld
      state "Completed" as FCompleted
      state "Cancelled" as FCancelled {
        [*] --> FCxQuiet
        state "Cancelled, nothing new since" as FCxQuiet
        state "Cancelled, new information since" as FCxNews
        FCxQuiet --> FCxNews : news for the patient
      }
      FNone --> FActive : create a follow-up
      FCompleted --> FActive : create a follow-up
      FCancelled --> FActive : create a follow-up
      FHeld --> FHeld : change the follow-up
      FActive --> FHeld : you stop the follow-up
      FHeld --> FActive : resume the follow-up
      FActive --> FCancelled : cancel the follow-up
      FHeld --> FCancelled : cancel the follow-up
      FActive --> FCompleted : complete the follow-up
      FHeld --> FCompleted : complete the follow-up
      FNone --> FActive : Coda finishes any work / may create a follow-up
      FCompleted --> FActive : Coda finishes any work / may create a follow-up
      FCxNews --> FActive : Coda finishes any work / may create a follow-up again on new information
      FWaiting --> FWaiting : Coda finishes any work / may revise the follow-up
      FDue --> FWaiting : Coda finishes the follow-up review / disposes of it with the next check
      FDue --> FCompleted : Coda finishes the follow-up review / disposes of it by completing it
      FWaiting --> FCompleted : Coda finishes the follow-up review / may complete the follow-up
      FActive --> FCompleted : Coda finishes other work [its review not in hand] / may complete the follow-up
      %% when not WHand@followup | reason: a due follow-up stays due until its own review disposes of it (RP-830, X1)
      %% never NothingLostDueFollowUp: Active follow-up.Due, its review owed & follow-up review not in hand.No follow-up review owed & Nothing left for you@followup -- A due follow-up always has its review in hand or its row on Today.
      %% never NoReviewWhenCompleted: follow-up review in hand & Completed -- A completed follow-up never has its review in hand.
      %% never NoReviewWhenCancelled: follow-up review in hand & Cancelled -- A cancelled follow-up never has its review in hand.
    }
    --
    %% Visit preparation: one visit at a time, owned by the practice schedule. Which visits are prepared and how
    %% far ahead is practice policy; it arrives as an event.
    state "Visit" as Visit {
      [*] --> VNone
      [*] --> VLater
      state "No visit scheduled" as VNone
      state "Visit ahead" as VAhead {
        [*] --> VLater
        state "Scheduled, not yet in preparation range" as VLater
        state "Upcoming, in preparation range" as VUpcoming
        VLater --> VUpcoming : the visit comes into preparation range
      }
      state "Visit over" as VOver
      state "Visit cancelled" as VCancel {
        [*] --> VCancelled
        state "Cancelled, its time not yet passed" as VCancelled
        state "Cancelled, its time has passed" as VCancelledOver
        VCancelled --> VCancelledOver : the visit ends
      }
      VAhead --> VOver : the visit ends
      VAhead --> VCancel : the visit is cancelled
      VAhead --> VLater : the visit is moved
      VNone --> VLater : a visit is scheduled
      VOver --> VLater : a visit is scheduled
      VCancel --> VLater : a visit is scheduled
    }
    --
    %% PX: an appointment without a patient mapping keeps its time and label with Preparation
    %% unavailable, no patient link and no clinical controls. An input from the practice.
    state "Visit patient mapping" as VisitMap {
      [*] --> VmMapped
      [*] --> VmUnmapped
      state "Visit linked to the patient" as VmMapped
      state "Preparation unavailable, no patient mapping" as VmUnmapped
    }
    --
    %% PX: a finished preparation always leaves a readable briefing; it is not acceptance
    %% of its recommendations, and it reaches you as a nudge only when Coda judges something new
    %% (a concern tied to the visit). A cancelled, moved or ended visit keeps it as history.
    state "Briefing" as Briefing {
      [*] --> BNone
      state "No briefing" as BNone
      state "Briefing ready for the upcoming visit" as BReady
      state "Earlier briefing, kept as history" as BOld
      BNone --> BReady : Coda finishes the visit preparation [visit ahead]
      %% when VAhead | reason: a briefing belongs to a visit still ahead (A7)
      BOld --> BReady : Coda finishes the visit preparation [visit ahead]
      %% when VAhead | reason: a briefing belongs to a visit still ahead (A7)
      BReady --> BReady : Coda finishes the visit preparation [visit ahead]
      %% when VAhead | reason: a briefing belongs to a visit still ahead (A7)
      BNone --> BOld : Coda finishes the visit preparation [visit passed]
      %% when not VAhead | reason: with no visit ahead, a briefing is kept only as history
      BReady --> BOld : Coda finishes the visit preparation [visit passed]
      %% when not VAhead | reason: with no visit ahead, a briefing is kept only as history
      BReady --> BOld : the visit ends
      BReady --> BOld : the visit is cancelled
      BReady --> BOld : the visit is moved
      %% never NoBriefingForPastVisit: Briefing ready for the upcoming visit & Visit over -- A briefing for a visit that has passed is history.
      %% never NoBriefingWhenCancelled: Briefing ready for the upcoming visit & Visit cancelled -- A cancelled visit's briefing is history.
      %% never NoNudgeForPastVisit: Tied to the upcoming visit & Visit over -- A nudge ends with its visit, unless it is an urgent one nobody opened.
      %% never NoPrepForCancelledVisit: visit preparation in hand & Visit cancelled -- Cancelling a visit ends its preparation at once.
    }
    --
    %% PX persistence: one private draft per physician and conversation, kept quietly (how it saves
    %% is the app's); Not saved stays visible with Retry; Discard is explicit (Dev 2026-10-26). Text a queue gives back comes
    %% here, including when access is lost or the session ends; nothing typed is lost (N3).
    state "Your draft" as Draft {
      [*] --> DEmpty
      state "Composer empty" as DEmpty
      state "Draft written" as DText {
        [*] --> DKept
        state "Draft kept quietly" as DKept
        state "Not saved, with Retry" as DNotSaved
        DKept --> DNotSaved : the draft fails to save
        DNotSaved --> DKept : the draft saves
        DNotSaved --> DKept : retry saving the draft
        DNotSaved --> DKept : type in the composer
        DNotSaved --> DKept : the transcript is inserted
        DNotSaved --> DKept : insert the transcript
      }
      DEmpty --> DKept : type in the composer
      DEmpty --> DKept : the transcript is inserted
      DEmpty --> DKept : insert the transcript
      DText --> DEmpty : send
      DText --> DEmpty : send to steer the answer
      DText --> DEmpty : send next
      DText --> DEmpty : discard the draft
      DEmpty --> DKept : remove a queued message
      DText --> DKept : remove a queued message
      DEmpty --> DKept : you lose clinical access [a message waits]
      %% when QQueued | reason: losing access returns waiting messages to the draft, so nothing typed is lost (N3)
      DText --> DKept : you lose clinical access [a message waits]
      %% when QQueued | reason: losing access returns waiting messages to the draft, so nothing typed is lost (N3)
    }
    --
    %% Several messages may wait, each editable; all attach to the next answer (RP-1542). How many is
    %% data. Losing access returns them to the draft.
    state "Queued messages" as Queue {
      [*] --> QNone
      state "Nothing queued" as QNone
      state "Messages queued for the next answer, each editable" as QQueued
      QNone --> QQueued : send next [answer in progress]
      %% when WActive@answer | reason: with no answer in progress the message starts one instead
      QQueued --> QQueued : send next [answer in progress]
      %% when WActive@answer | reason: with no answer in progress the message starts one instead
      QQueued --> QQueued : edit a queued message
      QQueued --> QQueued : remove a queued message / may keep others waiting
      QQueued --> QNone : remove a queued message
      QQueued --> QQueued : send a queued message now / may keep others waiting
      QQueued --> QNone : send a queued message now
      QQueued --> QNone : the queued message starts
      QQueued --> QNone : you lose clinical access
      %% never NoConversationWithIdentityOnly: Conversation & Identity only -- A conversation is clinical content.
      %% never NoConversationWithoutAccess: Conversation & Cannot see the patient -- A conversation is clinical content.
    }
    --
    %% Feedback on one completed communication, private to you and append-only: a flip keeps the old
    %% revision in history and starts empty details; there is no withdrawal (px.md:749-756).
    state "Your feedback" as Feedback {
      [*] --> FbNone
      state "Not rated" as FbNone
      state "Rated helpful" as FbUp
      state "Rated not helpful" as FbDown
      FbNone --> FbUp : rate the message up
      FbNone --> FbDown : rate the message down
      FbDown --> FbUp : rate the message up
      FbUp --> FbDown : rate the message down
    }
    --
    state "Your feedback details" as FbDetails {
      [*] --> FdEmpty
      state "No reasons or note" as FdEmpty
      state "Reasons or note saved" as FdSaved
      FdEmpty --> FdSaved : save the feedback details
      FdSaved --> FdSaved : save the feedback details
      FdSaved --> FdEmpty : rate the message up [flipping the rating]
      %% when FbDown | reason: a new rating starts with empty details
      FdSaved --> FdEmpty : rate the message down [flipping the rating]
      %% when FbUp | reason: a new rating starts with empty details
      %% never NoDetailsWithoutRating: Not rated & Reasons or note saved -- Details belong to a saved rating.
    }
    --
    %% Archive and Restore are physician organization only: neither stops work, clears attention, ends
    %% follow-ups or changes history, and reading keeps it archived (px.md:372-380). A deliberate start
    %% of the answer restores it in the same accepted command (runtime-protocol.md:500): Send, Resume,
    %% Try again (Resume's name after a failure, px.md:130) and Update (Dev 2026-10-24).
    state "Conversation list" as Organize {
      [*] --> CoActive
      state "In the active list" as CoActive
      state "Archived" as CoArchived
      CoActive --> CoArchived : archive the conversation
      CoArchived --> CoActive : restore the conversation
      CoArchived --> CoActive : undo the archive
      CoArchived --> CoActive : send
      CoArchived --> CoActive : resume the answer
      CoArchived --> CoActive : try the answer again
      CoArchived --> CoActive : update the answer with the newer records
      %% never NoAnswerWhileArchived: Archived & answer in hand.answer active -- An archived conversation has no answer running or owed.
      %% never NoPendingAnswerWhileArchived: Archived & answer in hand.answer stalled.answer waiting for the next opportunity, with Try again -- Archive excludes pending continuation.
      %% never NoQueueWhileArchived: Archived & Messages queued for the next answer, each editable -- An archived conversation has nothing queued.
    }
    --
    %% Updates (runtime-protocol.md:398-402): a finish that writes you something makes this patient's row
    %% for today new until you open it; a later communication that day is a new version. A quiet review,
    %% an outcome or a closed concern writes nothing and is never new.
    state "This patient's update today" as UpdateSeen {
      [*] --> UpNone
      state "Nothing written to you today" as UpNone
      state "Written to you, new" as UpNew
      state "Opened by you" as UpOpened
      UpNone --> UpNew : Coda finishes any work with an update for you
      UpOpened --> UpNew : Coda finishes any work with an update for you
      UpNew --> UpOpened : open an update
      UpNew --> UpNone : midnight passes
      UpOpened --> UpNone : midnight passes
    }
    --
    %% N2 (PM:640-711, Dev 2026-10-03): when a correction takes effect, whatever relied on the moved message keeps
    %% its place without its words (a concern keeps its row and Done; never sorts or alerts as now), for the
    %% physician and for Coda's own context. Withheld leaves only by a clean turn: the immediate re-review
    %% decides each item from the patient's own record. A review that fails or stalls leaves them withheld,
    %% with the existing Try again. Which items relied on it is the host's fact; the graph owns that it waits.
    state "What relied on a moved message" as Withheld {
      [*] --> WhNone
      state "Nothing withheld" as WhNone
      state "What relied on the moved message is withheld until Coda re-reviews" as WhWaiting
      WhNone --> WhWaiting : the correction's Undo ends
      WhWaiting --> WhNone : Coda finishes the patient review
      %% never MovedMessageConcernWithheld: About a patient message; stays with its message & No correction waiting on Undo.Another patient's message & Nothing withheld -- A concern about a moved message shows only after the re-review decides it.
      %% never NotAPatientConcernWithheld: About a patient message; stays with its message & No correction waiting on Undo.Not a patient, until the sender writes again & Nothing withheld -- A concern about a message marked not a patient shows only after the re-review decides it.
    }
    --
    %% PM section 8: only a revoked grant or an administrator's block needs Reconnect
    %% (PM-1275). Catching up and temporary sync failures are the channel's own and never shown, so the
    %% graph has none (Dev 2026-10-24); reconnect catches up without duplicates.
    state "Messaging channel" as Channel {
      [*] --> ChOff
      %% Not connected: never connected names nothing; a disconnected connection is one Coda isn't
      %% reading, named on Today, so the all-clear waits (patient-messaging.md:419-432).
      state "Channel not connected" as ChOff {
        [*] --> ChNever
        state "No channel connected" as ChNever
        state "Disconnected; Coda isn't reading it, named on Today" as ChDisconnected
      }
      state "Channel connected to the practice" as ChAccount {
        state "Connection" as ChConn {
          [*] --> ChConnecting
          state "Connecting the channel" as ChConnecting
          state "Channel live" as ChLive
          state "Channel needs reconnecting" as ChProblem
          state "Disconnecting" as ChDisconnecting
          ChConnecting --> ChLive : the provider authorizes the channel
          ChConnecting --> ChProblem : the provider refuses the channel
          ChLive --> ChProblem : the provider revokes access or an administrator blocks it
          ChProblem --> ChConnecting : reconnect the channel
          ChLive --> ChDisconnecting : disconnect the channel
          ChProblem --> ChDisconnecting : disconnect the channel
        }
        --
        %% PM-519: the messaging manager is whoever connected the account, until practice roles exist;
        %% it exists only while the channel is connected.
        state "Who manages messaging" as Manager {
          [*] --> MgrNo
          [*] --> MgrYes : connect the channel
          state "You manage the messaging connection" as MgrYes
          state "Someone else manages messaging" as MgrNo
        }
      }
      ChOff --> ChConnecting : connect the channel
      ChOff --> ChConnecting : someone else connects the channel
      ChDisconnecting --> ChDisconnected : the disconnect completes
    }
    --
    %% PM patient association (USER_SETTLED 2026-09-21): Coda's match is a suggestion a person confirms
    %% before the message enters the patient's evidence (PM-500); only known-sender rules link on
    %% arrival (PM-190). Not a patient leaves it unlinked until the sender writes again; corrections go
    %% forward only, by the messaging manager, with Undo for a few seconds; a missing roster entry is
    %% unsure, never not a patient.
    state "Patient message: match" as MsgLink {
      [*] --> MLFree
      %% A correction's Undo is a hold: while it shows, the patient's work waits to finish (PM:552-559).
      state "No correction waiting on Undo" as MLFree {
        [*] --> MLNone
        state "No message yet" as MLNone
        state "Coda is matching the message" as MLDeciding
        %% A6 (Dev): the one linking pass may also mark an unmatched message "looks urgent"; its row then
        %% leads Today as Now for everyone who sees it. Matching and confirmation are unchanged.
        state "Message to match" as MLWaiting {
          [*] --> MLWaitPlain
          state "Waiting to be matched" as MLWaitPlain
          state "Waiting to be matched, looks urgent; leads Today as Now" as MLWaitUrgent
        }
        state "Linked to the patient" as MLLinked
        state "Another patient's message" as MLOther
        state "Not a patient, until the sender writes again" as MLUnlinked
      }
      state "Moved to another patient, Undo shown" as MLUndoOther
      state "Marked not a patient, Undo shown" as MLUndoNot
      MLNone --> MLDeciding : a patient message arrives
      MLNone --> MLLinked : a message arrives from a known sender
      MLDeciding --> MLWaiting : Coda suggests a patient or is unsure
      MLDeciding --> MLWaitUrgent : Coda suggests a patient or is unsure / may mark it looks urgent
      MLDeciding --> MLUnlinked : Coda finds it is not a patient message
      MLWaiting --> MLUnlinked : Coda finds it is not a patient message
      MLWaiting --> MLLinked : confirm the match
      MLWaiting --> MLOther : confirm another patient
      MLWaiting --> MLUnlinked : mark the message not a patient
      MLUnlinked --> MLDeciding : the sender writes again
      MLUnlinked --> MLLinked : link the message to the patient
      MLOther --> MLLinked : link the message to the patient
      MLLinked --> MLLinked : the patient writes again
      MLLinked --> MLUndoOther : another patient chosen for the message
      MLLinked --> MLUndoNot : the message is marked not a patient
      MLUndoOther --> MLLinked : undo the correction
      MLUndoNot --> MLLinked : undo the correction
      MLUndoOther --> MLOther : the correction's Undo ends
      MLUndoNot --> MLUnlinked : the correction's Undo ends
      MLDeciding --> MLNone : the disconnect completes
      MLWaiting --> MLNone : the disconnect completes
      MLUnlinked --> MLNone : the disconnect completes
    }
    --
    %% PM-367: a message Coda couldn't read is never held out of sight; it puts the patient
    %% on Today until Coda reads it or you mark it Done.
    state "Patient message: read" as MsgRead {
      [*] --> MrOk
      state "Coda has read the conversation" as MrOk
      state "Coda couldn't read a message, on Today" as MrCant
      state "Couldn't read a message, marked done" as MrDone
      MrOk --> MrCant : Coda can't read a message from the patient
      MrDone --> MrCant : Coda can't read a message from the patient
      MrCant --> MrOk : Coda reads the message
      MrDone --> MrOk : Coda reads the message
      MrCant --> MrDone : mark the unread message done
      MrCant --> MrOk : the correction's Undo ends
      MrDone --> MrOk : the correction's Undo ends
      MrCant --> MrOk : the disconnect completes
      MrDone --> MrOk : the disconnect completes
    }
    --
    %% PM outcomes: a practice message sent outside Coda shows on the card at once, as a fact.
    state "Practice reply in the channel" as PracticeReply {
      [*] --> PrNone
      state "No practice reply since the patient wrote" as PrNone
      state "The practice replied in the channel" as PrShown
      PrNone --> PrShown : the practice replies in the channel
      PrNone --> PrShown : the channel sends the reply
      PrShown --> PrNone : the patient writes again
      PrShown --> PrNone : the disconnect completes
    }
    --
    %% PM reply card: one reply work item per conversation. Only a patient review or an
    %% asked reply drafts a reply (RP-2233). No reply needed has a brief Undo that reopens it exactly.
    %% Closing a reply because the practice answered is Coda's call and never a quiet finish (RP-392).
    %% A newer message's proposed reply wins over a No reply needed still showing Undo (RP-973). Your
    %% reply box lives inside the open reply work, so new reply work starts a fresh box (RP-461) and
    %% closing the reply never flips your edits (N10).
    state "Patient message: reply" as MsgReply {
      [*] --> MRRest
      state "No open reply" as MRRest {
        [*] --> MRNone
        state "No reply work" as MRNone
        state "Closed, no reply needed" as MRClosed
        state "Closed, the practice answered in the channel" as MRAnswered
        state "Closed, sent by Coda for you" as MRSent
      }
      state "Reply work open" as MROpen {
        state "Reply status" as MRStatus {
          [*] --> MRReady
          state "Reply ready" as MRReady {
            [*] --> MRToSend
            state "Ready to send or copy" as MRToSend
            state "Couldn't send, your text kept" as MRNotSent
          }
          state "Sending, as Coda for you" as MRSending
          state "Sending, as Coda for you; the patient wrote again" as MRSendingNew
          state "Reviewing a new message" as MRNewMsg
          state "Closed, no reply needed, Undo shown" as MRUndo
          MRReady --> MRNewMsg : the patient writes again
          MRReady --> MRUndo : mark no reply needed
          MRNewMsg --> MRUndo : mark no reply needed
          MRUndo --> MRReady : undo no reply needed
          MRNewMsg --> MRReady : Coda finishes the patient review / may propose a newer reply
          MRUndo --> MRNewMsg : the patient writes again
          MRNewMsg --> MRReady : Coda finishes the asked reply
          MRUndo --> MRReady : Coda finishes the asked reply
          MRReady --> MRSending : send the reply
          MRNewMsg --> MRSendingNew : send the reply
          MRSending --> MRSendingNew : the patient writes again
          MRSending --> MRNotSent : the channel can't send the reply
          MRSendingNew --> MRNewMsg : the channel can't send the reply
        }
        --
        %% PM reply card: your private draft for this reply. Untouched text follows Coda's newest;
        %% edited text stays yours with Coda's update offered; Restore my version is one restore point.
        state "Your reply text" as ReplyText {
          [*] --> RtFollow
          state "Untouched, shows Coda's newest text" as RtFollow
          state "Your edited reply" as RtEdited
          state "Your reply, with Coda's update offered" as RtOffered
          state "Coda's text replaced yours, Restore available" as RtRestorable
          RtFollow --> RtEdited : edit the reply
          RtEdited --> RtEdited : edit the reply
          RtOffered --> RtOffered : edit the reply
          RtRestorable --> RtEdited : edit the reply
          RtEdited --> RtOffered : Coda finishes the patient review / may offer Coda's update
          RtEdited --> RtOffered : Coda finishes the asked reply
          RtOffered --> RtRestorable : use Coda's update
          RtRestorable --> RtEdited : restore my version
          RtFollow --> RtRestorable : Coda finishes the reply revision
          RtEdited --> RtRestorable : Coda finishes the reply revision
          RtOffered --> RtRestorable : Coda finishes the reply revision
          RtRestorable --> RtRestorable : Coda finishes the reply revision
        }
        --
        %% A reply is new until you open it, and new again only when its own words change: another
        %% message arrives, or Coda writes a newer draft (runtime-protocol.md:282-284, px.md:165).
        state "Who has opened the reply" as ReplySeen {
          [*] --> RsNew
          state "New to you" as RsNew
          state "Opened by you, unchanged since" as RsOpened
          RsNew --> RsOpened : open the reply
          RsOpened --> RsNew : the patient writes again
          RsOpened --> RsNew : Coda finishes the patient review / may propose a newer reply
          RsOpened --> RsNew : Coda finishes the patient review / may offer Coda's update
          RsOpened --> RsNew : Coda finishes the asked reply
          RsOpened --> RsNew : Coda finishes the reply revision
        }
      }
      MRNone --> MRReady : Coda finishes the patient review [a linked message] / may propose a reply
      %% when MLLinked | reason: only a message linked to this patient is this patient's evidence (PM-500)
      MRRest --> MRReady : Coda finishes the asked reply [a linked message]
      %% when MLLinked | reason: only a message linked to this patient is this patient's evidence (PM-500)
      MRUndo --> MRClosed : the no-reply Undo ends
      MRClosed --> MRNone : the patient writes again
      MRAnswered --> MRNone : the patient writes again
      MRSent --> MRNone : the patient writes again
      MRSending --> MRSent : the channel sends the reply
      MRSendingNew --> MRNone : the channel sends the reply
      MRReady --> MRAnswered : Coda finishes the patient review [the practice replied] / may close the reply as answered
      %% when PrShown | reason: a reply closes as answered only after a practice message in that conversation (RP-392)
      MRNewMsg --> MRAnswered : Coda finishes the patient review [the practice replied] / may close the reply as answered
      %% when PrShown | reason: a reply closes as answered only after a practice message in that conversation (RP-392)
      MROpen --> MRNone : the correction's Undo ends
      MRAnswered --> MRNone : the correction's Undo ends
      MRClosed --> MRNone : the correction's Undo ends
      MRSent --> MRNone : the correction's Undo ends
      MROpen --> MRNone : the disconnect completes
      %% never NoReplyWhileMatching: No correction waiting on Undo.Coda is matching the message & Reply work open -- An unmatched message has no reply for this patient.
      %% never NoReplyForWaitingMatch: No correction waiting on Undo.Message to match & Reply work open -- A message waiting for a match has no reply for this patient.
      %% never NoReplyForOtherPatient: No correction waiting on Undo.Another patient's message & Reply work open -- A moved message never keeps this patient's reply.
      %% never NoReplyForNotAPatient: No correction waiting on Undo.Not a patient, until the sender writes again & Reply work open -- Not a patient keeps the conversation out of patient work.
      %% never NoAskForOtherPatient: No correction waiting on Undo.Another patient's message & asked reply in hand -- A moved message's asked reply stops.
      %% never NoRevisionWithoutReply: reply revision in hand.reply revision active & No open reply -- A revision runs only while its reply is open.
    }
  }
